#: manual/api/ball_float.md:146
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty and bounded, $f$ is defined and continuous on $\\boldsymbol{x}$, and $\\boldsymbol{y}$ is bounded"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空且有界，$f$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上有定义且连续，并且 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 有界"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:147
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty, $f$ is defined on $\\boldsymbol{x}$ and its restriction to $\\boldsymbol{x}$ is continuous"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空，$f$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上有定义，且其在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上的限制连续"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:148
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty and $f$ is defined on $\\boldsymbol{x}$"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空，且 $f$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上有定义"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:149
msgid "nothing is known"
msgstr "一无所知"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:150
msgid "the value is NaI"
msgstr "值为 NaI"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:152
msgid "Each property implies the ones below it, which is why the decorations are totally ordered. `Show` prints the lower-case IEEE 1788 names `com`, `dac`, `def`, `trv`, `ill`."
msgstr "每个性质都蕴含其下方的性质，因此装饰是全序的。`Show` 输出 IEEE 1788 的小写名称 `com`、`dac`、`def`、`trv`、`ill`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:158
msgid "`OverlapState` is the result of `overlap_state`: the IEEE 1788 classification of the relative position of two intervals."
msgstr "`OverlapState` 是 `overlap_state` 的结果：IEEE 1788 对两个区间相对位置的分类。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:183
msgid "The constructors correspond to the IEEE 1788 states `bothEmpty`, `firstEmpty`, `secondEmpty`, `before`, `meets`, `overlaps`, `starts`, `containedBy`, `finishes`, `equal`, `after`, `metBy`, `overlappedBy`, `startedBy`, `contains` and `finishedBy`; `OverlapsState`, `EqualIntervals` and `ContainsInterval` carry a suffix only to avoid clashing with method names. `Undefined` is returned only by the decorated version when an operand is NaI."
msgstr "这些构造子对应 IEEE 1788 的状态 `bothEmpty`、`firstEmpty`、`secondEmpty`、`before`、`meets`、`overlaps`、`starts`、`containedBy`、`finishes`、`equal`、`after`、`metBy`、`overlappedBy`、`startedBy`、`contains` 和 `finishedBy`；`OverlapsState`、`EqualIntervals` 和 `ContainsInterval` 带有后缀，只是为了避免与方法名冲突。仅当操作数为 NaI 时，装饰版本才会返回 `Undefined`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:192
msgid "`BallContext` describes a target binary format: a precision in bits and an exponent range $[e_{\\min}, e_{\\max}]$."
msgstr "`BallContext` 描述一个目标二进制格式：以位为单位的精度和指数范围 $[e_{\\min}, e_{\\max}]$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:201
msgid "$e_{\\min}$ and $e_{\\max}$ follow IEEE 754: a finite nonzero value $v$ with $2^{e} \\le |v| < 2^{e+1}$ is in range when $e \\le e_{\\max}$, and it is normal when $e \\ge e_{\\min}$. See [Contexts and flags](#contexts-and-flags)."
msgstr "$e_{\\min}$ 和 $e_{\\max}$ 遵循 IEEE 754：满足 $2^{e} \\le |v| < 2^{e+1}$ 的有限非零值 $v$，当 $e \\le e_{\\max}$ 时在范围内，当 $e \\ge e_{\\min}$ 时为正规数。参见[上下文与标志](#contexts-and-flags)。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:207
msgid "`BallFlags` records the conditions raised while rounding an interval into a `BallContext`."
msgstr "`BallFlags` 记录将区间舍入到某个 `BallContext` 时触发的条件。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:218
msgid "`inexact` is set when an endpoint (or, for `midpoint_ctx`, the midpoint) changed; `overflow` when it was beyond $e_{\\max}$; `underflow` when it is tiny and inexact, as IEEE 754 defines it (see [`BallFloat::apply_ctx`](#ballfloatapply_ctx)). The fields are readable; the accessor methods are listed under [`BallFlags::new`](#ballflagsnew-ballflagscombine-ballflagsinexact-ballflagsoverflow-ballflagsunderflow)."
msgstr "当端点（对 `midpoint_ctx` 而言是中点）发生改变时设置 `inexact`；当其超出 $e_{\\max}$ 时设置 `overflow`；当其为微小值且不精确时设置 `underflow`，与 IEEE 754 的定义一致（参见 [`BallFloat::apply_ctx`](#ballfloatapply_ctx)）。这些字段可读；访问器方法列于 [`BallFlags::new`](#ballflagsnew-ballflagscombine-ballflagsinexact-ballflagsoverflow-ballflagsunderflow) 之下。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:224
#: manual/api/ball_float_checked.md:59
#: manual/api/bin_float_checked.md:61
#: manual/api/decimal_checked.md:67
#: manual/api/decimal_gda_checked.md:66
msgid "Construction"
msgstr "构造"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:228
msgid "`BallFloat::new` builds the interval $[c - r, c + r]$ from a center and a radius, enlarged so that it is exact at the requested precision."
msgstr "`BallFloat::new` 由中心和半径构建区间 $[c - r, c + r]$，并适当扩大以使其在所请求的精度下可精确表示。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:235
msgid "The default precision is the larger of the precisions of `center` and `radius`. With $p$ that precision, the stored interval is"
msgstr "默认精度是 `center` 与 `radius` 精度中的较大者。记该精度为 $p$，则存储的区间为"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:244
msgid "which contains $[c - r, c + r]$ (proof in the [design page](../design/ball_float.md#from-midpointradius-to-endpoints)). The endpoints $\\tilde c \\pm R$ are formed exactly, so they may carry more than $p$ bits. Aborts when `center` or `radius` is not finite or when `radius` is negative. A precision below 1 is treated as 1."
msgstr "它包含 $[c - r, c + r]$（证明见[设计文档](../design/ball_float.md#from-midpointradius-to-endpoints)）。端点 $\\tilde c \\pm R$ 是精确构成的，因此其位数可能多于 $p$。当 `center` 或 `radius` 非有限，或 `radius` 为负时中止。小于 1 的精度按 1 处理。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:250
msgid "When $c$ already has at most $p$ bits and $r = 0$, the result is the singleton $\\{c\\}$. When $c$ needs more than $p$ bits, the rounding error of the center is added to the radius on *both* sides, so the interval is wider than $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(c - r), \\operatorname{RU}_p(c + r)]$; use `from_bounds` for the tightest enclosure of known bounds."
msgstr "当 $c$ 已至多有 $p$ 位且 $r = 0$ 时，结果为单点集 $\\{c\\}$。当 $c$ 需要多于 $p$ 位时，中心的舍入误差会在*两侧*都加到半径上，因此区间比 $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(c - r), \\operatorname{RU}_p(c + r)]$ 更宽；若要得到已知界的最紧包络，请使用 `from_bounds`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:256
msgid "`BallFloat::from_bounds` and `BallFloat::try_from_bounds`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_bounds` 与 `BallFloat::try_from_bounds`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:258
msgid "`BallFloat::from_bounds` builds the interval $[\\underline{x}, \\overline{x}]$ from its endpoints, rounded outward to the requested precision."
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_bounds` 由端点构建区间 $[\\underline{x}, \\overline{x}]$，并向外舍入到所请求的精度。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:266
msgid "The default precision is the larger of the endpoint precisions. Infinite endpoints build unbounded intervals: `from_bounds(-inf, +inf)` is Entire. The inputs are invalid when an endpoint is NaN, the lower endpoint is $+\\infty$, the upper endpoint is $-\\infty$, or $\\underline{x} > \\overline{x}$; `from_bounds` aborts and `try_from_bounds` returns a domain error. There is no way to build Empty from bounds; use `BallFloat::empty`."
msgstr "默认精度是两个端点精度中的较大者。无穷端点构建无界区间：`from_bounds(-inf, +inf)` 即 Entire。当某个端点为 NaN、下端点为 $+\\infty$、上端点为 $-\\infty$ 或 $\\underline{x} > \\overline{x}$ 时，输入无效；此时 `from_bounds` 中止，`try_from_bounds` 返回定义域错误。无法由端点构建 Empty；请使用 `BallFloat::empty`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:283
msgid "`BallFloat::exact` and `BallFloat::try_exact`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::exact` 与 `BallFloat::try_exact`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:285
msgid "`BallFloat::exact` builds the singleton $\\{x\\}$ of a finite `BinFloat`."
msgstr "`BallFloat::exact` 构建有限 `BinFloat` 的单点集 $\\{x\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:292
msgid "The default precision is that of `x`. When `x` has more significant bits than the requested precision, the singleton is rounded outward to the two-point interval $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(x), \\operatorname{RU}_p(x)]$. A non-finite `x` aborts `exact` and makes `try_exact` return a domain error."
msgstr "默认精度为 `x` 的精度。当 `x` 的有效位数多于所请求的精度时，单点集会向外舍入为两点区间 $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(x), \\operatorname{RU}_p(x)]$。非有限的 `x` 会使 `exact` 中止，并使 `try_exact` 返回定义域错误。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:297
msgid "`BallFloat::from_int` and `BallFloat::from_coefficient`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_int` 与 `BallFloat::from_coefficient`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:299
msgid "`BallFloat::from_int` and `BallFloat::from_coefficient` build an enclosure of an integer."
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_int` 和 `BallFloat::from_coefficient` 构建整数的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:307
msgid "The default precision is 16. `from_coefficient` takes a non-negative `BinCoeff` magnitude and a separate sign. The integer is converted to a `BinFloat` exactly and then passed to `exact`, so the result is the singleton $\\{n\\}$ when $n$ fits in $p$ bits and the two-point interval $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(n), \\operatorname{RU}_p(n)]$ otherwise. Either way it contains $n$. Pass a precision at least as large as the bit length of the integer to get a singleton."
msgstr "默认精度为 16。`from_coefficient` 接受一个非负的 `BinCoeff` 绝对值和一个单独的符号。整数先被精确转换为 `BinFloat`，再传给 `exact`，因此当 $n$ 能用 $p$ 位表示时结果为单点集 $\\{n\\}$，否则为两点区间 $[\\operatorname{RD}_p(n), \\operatorname{RU}_p(n)]$。无论哪种情况结果都包含 $n$。要得到单点集，请传入不小于该整数位长的精度。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:315
msgid "`BallFloat::from_double`, `BallFloat::try_from_double`, `BallFloat::from_float` and `BallFloat::try_from_float`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_double`、`BallFloat::try_from_double`、`BallFloat::from_float` 和 `BallFloat::try_from_float`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:317
msgid "These functions build the singleton of the exact binary value of a `Double` or `Float`."
msgstr "这些函数构建 `Double` 或 `Float` 的精确二进制值的单点集。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:327
msgid "Default precisions are 53 and 24. The conversion to `BinFloat` is exact; a smaller requested precision rounds the singleton outward. NaN and infinities abort the plain forms and are domain errors for the `try_` forms. The result encloses the binary value, not the decimal literal it was written as: `from_double(0.1)` does not contain $1/10$."
msgstr "默认精度分别为 53 和 24。到 `BinFloat` 的转换是精确的；若请求的精度更小，则单点集会向外舍入。NaN 和无穷会使普通形式中止，对 `try_` 形式则是定义域错误。结果包络的是二进制值，而不是书写时的十进制字面量：`from_double(0.1)` 不包含 $1/10$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:333
msgid "`BallFloat::whole` and `BallFloat::empty`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::whole` 与 `BallFloat::empty`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:335
msgid "`BallFloat::whole` returns Entire and `BallFloat::empty` returns Empty."
msgstr "`BallFloat::whole` 返回 Entire，`BallFloat::empty` 返回 Empty。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:342
msgid "The default precision is 53."
msgstr "默认精度为 53。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:344
msgid "Observers"
msgstr "观察函数"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:346
msgid "`BallFloat::lower_bound` and `BallFloat::upper_bound`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::lower_bound` 与 `BallFloat::upper_bound`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:348
msgid "`lower_bound` and `upper_bound` return the stored endpoints."
msgstr "`lower_bound` 和 `upper_bound` 返回存储的端点。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:355
msgid "For an unbounded side the endpoint is an infinity. For Empty they return $+\\infty$ and $-\\infty$ respectively, so test `is_empty` first."
msgstr "在无界的一侧，端点是无穷。对于 Empty，二者分别返回 $+\\infty$ 和 $-\\infty$，因此请先检查 `is_empty`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:358
msgid "`BallFloat::center` and `BallFloat::radius`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::center` 与 `BallFloat::radius`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:360
msgid "`center` and `radius` return the midpoint–radius view of a bounded interval."
msgstr "`center` 和 `radius` 返回有界区间的中点–半径视图。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:367
msgid "`center` is $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$ and `radius` is $(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})/2$. Both are dyadic, so they are computed exactly (the radius is rounded up only if it underflows the exponent range), and $[\\text{center} - \\text{radius}, \\text{center} + \\text{radius}]$ is the stored interval. Both abort on Empty and on unbounded intervals."
msgstr "`center` 为 $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$，`radius` 为 $(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})/2$。二者都是二进有理数，因此均精确计算（仅当半径低于指数范围下溢时才向上舍入），并且 $[\\text{center} - \\text{radius}, \\text{center} + \\text{radius}]$ 就是存储的区间。二者在 Empty 和无界区间上均会中止。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:373
msgid "[!NOTE] For bounded intervals whose endpoints are more than about $2^{16}$ binary orders of magnitude apart, neither value is exact: the smaller endpoint is replaced by a sticky surrogate below the last bit of the larger one (see the [design page](../design/ball_float.md#far-addends-bound-endpoint-sums-by-precision)), rounded to nearest for `center` and upward for `radius`. The pair then describes the stored set only approximately."
msgstr "[!NOTE] 对于端点在二进制数量级上相差超过约 $2^{16}$ 的有界区间，两个值都不是精确的：较小的端点会被替换为一个低于较大端点最末位的粘滞替代值（参见[设计文档](../design/ball_float.md#far-addends-bound-endpoint-sums-by-precision)），对 `center` 就近舍入，对 `radius` 向上舍入。此时这对值只能近似地描述所存储的集合。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:383
msgid "`midpoint` returns the center rounded to nearest at the interval's precision."
msgstr "`midpoint` 返回以区间精度就近舍入后的中心。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:389
msgid "Entire has midpoint 0. Empty and half-bounded intervals abort."
msgstr "Entire 的中点为 0。Empty 和半无界区间会中止。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:391
msgid "`BallFloat::width` and `BallFloat::radius_extended`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::width` 与 `BallFloat::radius_extended`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:393
msgid "`width` returns $\\operatorname{RU}_p(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})$ and `radius_extended` returns the radius rounded up to the interval's precision."
msgstr "`width` 返回 $\\operatorname{RU}_p(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})$，`radius_extended` 返回向上舍入到区间精度的半径。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:401
msgid "Both return 0 for Empty and $+\\infty$ for unbounded intervals instead of aborting. Both are upper bounds of the exact value."
msgstr "二者对 Empty 返回 0，对无界区间返回 $+\\infty$，而不会中止。二者都是精确值的上界。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:404
msgid "`BallFloat::magnitude` and `BallFloat::mignitude`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::magnitude` 与 `BallFloat::mignitude`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:406
msgid "`magnitude` returns $\\sup\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$ and `mignitude` returns $\\inf\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$."
msgstr "`magnitude` 返回 $\\sup\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$，`mignitude` 返回 $\\inf\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:414
msgid "For a non-empty interval,"
msgstr "对于非空区间，"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:426
msgid "because $|\\xi|$ is convex, so its maximum over an interval is at an endpoint, and it is monotone on each side of 0. Both are exact. Empty gives 0 for both (IEEE 1788 leaves them undefined there); `magnitude` of an unbounded interval is $+\\infty$."
msgstr "这是因为 $|\\xi|$ 是凸函数，其在区间上的最大值位于端点处，并且它在 0 的两侧各自单调。二者都是精确的。Empty 对二者都给出 0（IEEE 1788 在此处未作定义）；无界区间的 `magnitude` 为 $+\\infty$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:444
msgid "`BallFloat::precision`, `BallFloat::classify` and `BallFloat::sign`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::precision`、`BallFloat::classify` 与 `BallFloat::sign`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:446
msgid "`precision` returns the precision tag; `classify` and `sign` describe the interval in the vocabulary of scalar floating-point types."
msgstr "`precision` 返回精度标记；`classify` 和 `sign` 用标量浮点类型的术语描述区间。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:455
msgid "`classify` returns `NaN` for Empty, `Finite` for a bounded interval and `Infinity` for an unbounded one. `sign` returns `Positive` when $\\underline{x} > 0$, `Negative` when $\\overline{x} < 0$, and `Zero` otherwise: `Zero` means \"the interval contains 0\", not \"the interval is $\\{0\\}$\". `sign` aborts on Empty."
msgstr "`classify` 对 Empty 返回 `NaN`，对有界区间返回 `Finite`，对无界区间返回 `Infinity`。`sign` 在 $\\underline{x} > 0$ 时返回 `Positive`，在 $\\overline{x} < 0$ 时返回 `Negative`，否则返回 `Zero`：`Zero` 表示“区间包含 0”，而不是“区间为 $\\{0\\}$”。`sign` 在 Empty 上中止。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:463
msgid "These predicates test the shape of the set."
msgstr "这些谓词检测集合的形状。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:474
msgid "`is_bounded` and `is_common_interval` (the IEEE 1788 name) are the same: the interval is non-empty with two finite endpoints. `is_singleton` holds when $\\underline{x} = \\overline{x}$. `contains_zero` is false for Empty."
msgstr "`is_bounded` 与 `is_common_interval`（IEEE 1788 中的名称）相同：区间非空且两个端点均有限。当 $\\underline{x} = \\overline{x}$ 时 `is_singleton` 成立。对 Empty，`contains_zero` 为假。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:478
#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:437
msgid "Precision"
msgstr "精度"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:482
msgid "`with_precision` re-rounds an interval to a new precision without shrinking it."
msgstr "`with_precision` 将区间重新舍入到新的精度，且不会使其缩小。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:489
msgid "The endpoints are rounded outward: the lower bound toward $-\\infty$ and the upper bound toward $+\\infty$. `mode` is accepted for signature compatibility and is ignored, because outward rounding is the only direction that keeps the result an enclosure. Empty stays Empty with the new precision."
msgstr "端点向外取整：下界朝 $-\\infty$，上界朝 $+\\infty$。`mode` 仅为签名兼容而保留并被忽略，因为向外取整是唯一能让结果保持为包络的方向。Empty 仍为 Empty，并带上新精度。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:494
msgid "[!NOTE] The result is the tightest representable enclosure of the input, so widening the precision is exact and re-rounding at an unchanged precision is an identity. The center–radius rebuild this function used to perform is not an identity: if the exact center $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$ needs more than $p$ bits, both endpoints move outward by the rounding error of the center, so at 53 bits $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ became $[1 - 2^{-52}, 1 + 2^{-52}]$. `normalized`, `convex_hull` with an Empty operand, the checked capabilities (`div_checked`, `pow_nat_checked`, `pow_int_checked`) and the `pow_nat`/`pow_int` methods of `ball_float_checked` round endpoints the same way and do not widen a representable interval either."
msgstr "[!NOTE] 结果是输入的可表示最紧包络，因此加宽精度是精确的，在精度不变时重新取整是恒等操作。本函数过去采用的中心–半径重建并非恒等：若精确中心 $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$ 需要多于 $p$ 位，两个端点都会按中心的舍入误差向外移动，因此在 53 位下 $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ 曾变成 $[1 - 2^{-52}, 1 + 2^{-52}]$。`normalized`、带 Empty 操作数的 `convex_hull`、checked 能力（`div_checked`、`pow_nat_checked`、`pow_int_checked`）以及 `ball_float_checked` 的 `pow_nat`/`pow_int` 方法以同样的方式舍入端点，同样不会加宽可表示的区间。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:527
msgid "`normalized` normalizes the two endpoints (`BinFloat::normalized` removes trailing zero bits) and stores them at the interval's precision."
msgstr "`normalized` 规范化两个端点（`BinFloat::normalized` 去掉末尾的零位），并以区间的精度存储它们。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:534
msgid "The stored endpoints are already representable at that precision, so the result is the same set as the input: `normalized` of $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ at 53 bits is $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$, and the `@def.Floating` law \"normalizing keeps the value\" holds. Empty stays Empty."
msgstr "存储的端点在该精度下本就可表示，因此结果与输入是同一个集合：53 位下 $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ 的 `normalized` 就是 $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$，`@def.Floating` 定律“规范化保持值不变”成立。Empty 仍为 Empty。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:539
msgid "Set operations"
msgstr "集合运算"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:541
msgid "`BallFloat::intersection` and `BallFloat::convex_hull`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::intersection` 与 `BallFloat::convex_hull`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:543
msgid "`intersection` returns $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y}$ and `convex_hull` returns the smallest interval containing $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cup \\boldsymbol{y}$."
msgstr "`intersection` 返回 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y}$，`convex_hull` 返回包含 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cup \\boldsymbol{y}$ 的最小区间。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:551
msgid "For non-empty operands both are computed by endpoint `max`/`min` ($[\\max(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\min(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$ and $[\\min(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\max(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$), exact apart from the final outward rounding to the larger precision. Disjoint intervals intersect to Empty, and an Empty operand makes the intersection Empty. When one operand of `convex_hull` is Empty, the result is the other operand passed through `with_precision`, so it can be one ulp wider per side than that operand (see the warning under [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision))."
msgstr "对于非空操作数，二者都通过端点的 `max`/`min` 计算（$[\\max(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\min(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$ 和 $[\\min(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\max(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$），除最后向外舍入到较大精度外都是精确的。不相交的区间求交得到 Empty，有 Empty 操作数时交集为 Empty。当 `convex_hull` 的一个操作数为 Empty 时，结果是另一个操作数经过 `with_precision` 的结果，因此每侧可能比该操作数宽一个 ulp（参见 [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision) 下的警告）。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:561
msgid "`BallFloat::cancel_plus` and `BallFloat::cancel_minus`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::cancel_plus` 与 `BallFloat::cancel_minus`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:563
msgid "`cancel_minus(x, y)` is the IEEE 1788 cancellative subtraction: in exact arithmetic it returns the interval $\\boldsymbol{z}$ with $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = \\boldsymbol{x}$, which undoes a previous sum; `cancel_plus(x, y)` is `cancel_minus(x, -y)`."
msgstr "`cancel_minus(x, y)` 是 IEEE 1788 的消去减法：在精确算术下，它返回满足 $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = \\boldsymbol{x}$ 的区间 $\\boldsymbol{z}$，从而撤销先前的求和；`cancel_plus(x, y)` 即 `cancel_minus(x, -y)`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:573
msgid "For bounded operands `cancel_minus` is $[\\operatorname{RD}(\\underline{x} - \\underline{y}), \\operatorname{RU}(\\overline{x} - \\overline{y})]$. Indeed $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = [\\underline{y} + \\underline{z}, \\overline{y} + \\overline{z}]$, so $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = \\boldsymbol{x}$ forces $\\underline{z} = \\underline{x} - \\underline{y}$ and $\\overline{z} = \\overline{x} - \\overline{y}$, and this is an interval exactly when $w(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\ge w(\\boldsymbol{y})$. Because of the outward rounding, the computed $\\boldsymbol{z}$ satisfies $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} \\supseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$. When $w(\\boldsymbol{y}) > w(\\boldsymbol{x})$, when an operand is unbounded, or when only $\\boldsymbol{y}$ is empty, the result is Entire. Empty $\\boldsymbol{x}$ with bounded or empty $\\boldsymbol{y}$ gives Empty."
msgstr "对于有界操作数，`cancel_minus` 为 $[\\operatorname{RD}(\\underline{x} - \\underline{y}), \\operatorname{RU}(\\overline{x} - \\overline{y})]$。事实上 $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = [\\underline{y} + \\underline{z}, \\overline{y} + \\overline{z}]$，因此 $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} = \\boldsymbol{x}$ 迫使 $\\underline{z} = \\underline{x} - \\underline{y}$ 且 $\\overline{z} = \\overline{x} - \\overline{y}$，而它恰在 $w(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\ge w(\\boldsymbol{y})$ 时是一个区间。由于向外舍入，计算所得的 $\\boldsymbol{z}$ 满足 $\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z} \\supseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$。当 $w(\\boldsymbol{y}) > w(\\boldsymbol{x})$、有操作数无界或仅 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 为空时，结果为 Entire。$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 为空且 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 有界或为空时，结果为 Empty。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:600
msgid "Relations"
msgstr "关系"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:602
msgid "All relations are set relations of IEEE 1788; none of them is a total order. They never abort."
msgstr "所有关系都是 IEEE 1788 的集合关系；它们都不是全序。它们从不中止。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:607
msgid "`contains` tests whether a point belongs to the interval."
msgstr "`contains` 检测一个点是否属于该区间。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:613
msgid "It returns false for Empty and for a non-finite point (an unbounded interval contains all sufficiently large reals, but not $\\pm\\infty$ or NaN). The trait method `@lf_arith.Contains::contains` instead takes two intervals and tests inclusion; see [Enclosure relations](#arithmeticcontains-arithmeticoverlaps-arithmeticdefinitelylt-arithmeticdefinitelyle-arithmeticmaybeeq)."
msgstr "对 Empty 和非有限的点，它返回假（无界区间包含所有足够大的实数，但不包含 $\\pm\\infty$ 或 NaN）。trait 方法 `@lf_arith.Contains::contains` 则接受两个区间并检测包含关系；参见[包络关系](#arithmeticcontains-arithmeticoverlaps-arithmeticdefinitelylt-arithmeticdefinitelyle-arithmeticmaybeeq)。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:621
msgid "These test inclusion, inclusion in the interior, equality and disjointness of sets."
msgstr "这些函数检测集合的包含、内部包含、相等与不相交。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:631
msgid "`x.subset(y)` is $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{y}$, that is $\\underline{y} \\le \\underline{x}$ and $\\overline{x} \\le \\overline{y}$. `x.interior(y)` is $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq \\operatorname{int} \\boldsymbol{y}$: each endpoint comparison is strict, except that two equal infinite endpoints count as interior (the interior of $[a, +\\infty)$ is $(a, +\\infty)$, so Entire is interior to itself). Empty is a subset of, interior to and disjoint from every interval. `set_equal` ignores the precision tag and the representation of the endpoints."
msgstr "`x.subset(y)` 即 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{y}$，也就是 $\\underline{y} \\le \\underline{x}$ 且 $\\overline{x} \\le \\overline{y}$。`x.interior(y)` 即 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq \\operatorname{int} \\boldsymbol{y}$：每个端点比较都是严格的，但两个相等的无穷端点视为位于内部（$[a, +\\infty)$ 的内部为 $(a, +\\infty)$，因此 Entire 在其自身内部）。Empty 是任何区间的子集、位于任何区间内部，并且与任何区间不相交。`set_equal` 忽略精度标记和端点的表示方式。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:642
msgid "`overlaps` tests whether two intervals share a point; `maybe_eq` is the same relation read as \"the two unknown points may be equal\"; `separated_from` is its negation."
msgstr "`overlaps` 检测两个区间是否有公共点；`maybe_eq` 是同一关系，但解读为“两个未知点可能相等”；`separated_from` 是其否定。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:652
msgid ""
"For non-empty operands `overlaps` is $\\underline{x} \\le \\overline{y} \\wedge \\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}$, which is $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\emptyset$. `overlaps` is false and `separated_from` is true when an operand is Empty."
msgstr ""
"对于非空操作数，`overlaps` 为 $\\underline{x} \\le \\overline{y} \\wedge \\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}$，即 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\emptyset$。当有操作数为 Empty 时，`overlaps` 为假，`separated_from` 为真。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:659
msgid "These hold when the order holds for every pair of points."
msgstr "当所有点对都满足该序关系时，这些关系才成立。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:667
msgid "`x.definitely_lt(y)` is $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$, `definitely_le` is $\\overline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$ and `definitely_gt` is $\\underline{x} > \\overline{y}$. All three are false when an operand is Empty (unlike `precedes`, which is vacuously true), so a `true` answer is always backed by at least one pair of points."
msgstr "`x.definitely_lt(y)` 即 $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$，`definitely_le` 即 $\\overline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$，`definitely_gt` 即 $\\underline{x} > \\overline{y}$。当有操作数为 Empty 时三者均为假（与 `precedes` 不同，后者此时空真），因此 `true` 的回答总有至少一对点作为依据。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:675
msgid "These are the order relations of IEEE 1788."
msgstr "这些是 IEEE 1788 的序关系。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:684
msgid "For non-empty operands:"
msgstr "对于非空操作数："

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:686
msgid "Relation"
msgstr "关系"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:686
msgid "Set definition"
msgstr "集合定义"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:686
msgid "Condition"
msgstr "条件"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:688
msgid "$\\forall\\xi\\,\\exists\\eta: \\xi \\le \\eta$ and $\\forall\\eta\\,\\exists\\xi: \\xi \\le \\eta$"
msgstr "$\\forall\\xi\\,\\exists\\eta: \\xi \\le \\eta$ 且 $\\forall\\eta\\,\\exists\\xi: \\xi \\le \\eta$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:688
msgid "$\\underline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$ and $\\overline{x} \\le \\overline{y}$"
msgstr "$\\underline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$ 且 $\\overline{x} \\le \\overline{y}$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:689
msgid "the same with $<$"
msgstr "同上，改用 $<$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:689
msgid "$\\underline{x} < \\underline{y}$ (or both $-\\infty$) and $\\overline{x} < \\overline{y}$ (or both $+\\infty$)"
msgstr "$\\underline{x} < \\underline{y}$（或二者均为 $-\\infty$）且 $\\overline{x} < \\overline{y}$（或二者均为 $+\\infty$）"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:693
msgid "With Empty: `less` and `strictly_less` hold only when both are Empty; `precedes` and `strictly_precedes` hold when either is Empty."
msgstr "涉及 Empty 时：`less` 和 `strictly_less` 仅当两者均为 Empty 时成立；`precedes` 和 `strictly_precedes` 在任一者为 Empty 时成立。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:698
msgid "`overlap_state` classifies the relative position of two intervals."
msgstr "`overlap_state` 对两个区间的相对位置进行分类。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:704
msgid "The result is one of the sixteen states of [`OverlapState`](#overlapstate) other than `Undefined`; it is computed from the comparisons of the four endpoints, testing equal endpoints first, so a singleton that coincides with an endpoint of the other interval gives `Starts`, `Finishes`, `StartedBy` or `FinishedBy` rather than `Meets` or `MetBy`, as IEEE 1788 requires."
msgstr "结果是 [`OverlapState`](#overlapstate) 中除 `Undefined` 以外的十六种状态之一；它由四个端点之间的比较计算得出，并先检测相等的端点，因此与另一区间某个端点重合的单点集会按 IEEE 1788 的要求给出 `Starts`、`Finishes`、`StartedBy` 或 `FinishedBy`，而不是 `Meets` 或 `MetBy`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:726
#: manual/api/ball_float_checked.md:218
#: manual/api/bin_float_checked.md:183
msgid "Arithmetic"
msgstr "算术"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:730
msgid "The four basic operations return the outward-rounded hull of $\\{\\xi \\circ \\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}\\}$; they are also available as the operators `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`."
msgstr "四则基本运算返回 $\\{\\xi \\circ \\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}\\}$ 向外舍入后的包；它们也可以通过运算符 `+`、`-`、`*`、`/` 使用。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:741
msgid "The result precision is the larger operand precision; an Empty operand gives Empty. Endpoint formulas:"
msgstr "结果精度为操作数中较大的精度；有 Empty 操作数时结果为 Empty。端点公式如下："

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:752
msgid "with $0 \\cdot \\infty$ taken as 0 in $S$ (a zero endpoint times an unbounded side contributes 0). The sums and products are formed exactly and rounded once. For bounded operands the signs select the products that can be extremal: two when both operands have constant sign, four (the minimum of $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$ and $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$, the maximum of $\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ and $\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$) when either operand has 0 in its interior. The design page proves the [sign-case table](../design/ball_float.md#endpoint-formulas)."
msgstr "其中在 $S$ 中将 $0 \\cdot \\infty$ 取为 0（零端点乘以无界的一侧贡献 0）。各和与积都精确构造，并只舍入一次。对于有界操作数，由符号选出可能取极值的乘积：两个操作数符号都不变时取两个，任一操作数在内部含 0 时取四个（$\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$ 与 $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ 的最小值，$\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ 与 $\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$ 的最大值）。设计文档证明了[符号情形表](../design/ball_float.md#endpoint-formulas)。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:761
msgid ""
"Division follows IEEE 1788: $\\boldsymbol{x} / \\boldsymbol{y}$ is the hull of $\\{\\xi/\\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}, \\eta \\n"
"e 0\\}$."
msgstr ""
"除法遵循 IEEE 1788：$\\boldsymbol{x} / \\boldsymbol{y}$ 是 $\\{\\xi/\\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}, \\eta \\n"
"e 0\\}$ 的包。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:764
msgid "Divisor $\\boldsymbol{y}$"
msgstr "除数 $\\boldsymbol{y}$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:764
#: manual/api/bin_float.md:46
#: manual/api/decimal_checked.md:281
#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:72
#: manual/performance_audit.md:122
msgid "Result"
msgstr "结果"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:766
msgid "$[\\operatorname{RD}\\min Q, \\operatorname{RU}\\max Q]$ over the endpoint quotients $Q$"
msgstr "$[\\operatorname{RD}\\min Q, \\operatorname{RU}\\max Q]$，其中 $Q$ 取遍端点之商"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:767
msgid "Empty"
msgstr "Empty"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:768
msgid "Entire, unless $\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$"
msgstr "Entire，除非 $\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:769
msgid "$[0, \\overline{y}]$ or $[\\underline{y}, 0]$"
msgstr "$[0, \\overline{y}]$ 或 $[\\underline{y}, 0]$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:769
msgid "half-unbounded (see below), or Entire when $\\underline{x} < 0 < \\overline{x}$"
msgstr "半无界（见下文），当 $\\underline{x} < 0 < \\overline{x}$ 时为 Entire"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:771
msgid "When the divisor touches 0 at one end, the quotient is unbounded on one side: for example $[1, 2]/[0, 4] = [1/4, +\\infty)$ and $[-2, -1]/[0, 4] = (-\\infty, -1/4]$. A dividend equal to $\\{0\\}$ gives $\\{0\\}$ for any divisor other than $\\{0\\}$. Each selected quotient is computed by one directed division at the result precision."
msgstr "当除数在一端触及 0 时，商在一侧无界：例如 $[1, 2]/[0, 4] = [1/4, +\\infty)$，$[-2, -1]/[0, 4] = (-\\infty, -1/4]$。被除数等于 $\\{0\\}$ 时，对除 $\\{0\\}$ 以外的任何除数都得到 $\\{0\\}$。每个选出的商都在结果精度下通过一次定向除法计算。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:791
msgid "`BallFloat::neg` and `BallFloat::abs`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::neg` 与 `BallFloat::abs`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:793
msgid "`neg` returns $[-\\overline{x}, -\\underline{x}]$ and `abs` returns $\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$."
msgstr "`neg` 返回 $[-\\overline{x}, -\\underline{x}]$，`abs` 返回 $\\{|\\xi| : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:801
msgid "`abs` is $\\boldsymbol{x}$ when $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$, $-\\boldsymbol{x}$ when $\\overline{x} \\le 0$, and $[0, \\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{x}]$ otherwise. Both are exact. `neg` is also the unary operator `-`."
msgstr "当 $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$ 时 `abs` 为 $\\boldsymbol{x}$，当 $\\overline{x} \\le 0$ 时为 $-\\boldsymbol{x}$，否则为 $[0, \\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{x}]$。二者都是精确的。`neg` 也是一元运算符 `-`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:807
msgid "`reciprocal` returns $1/\\boldsymbol{x}$ with the division rules above."
msgstr "`reciprocal` 按上述除法规则返回 $1/\\boldsymbol{x}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:813
msgid "`BallFloat::square` and `BallFloat::pown`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::square` 与 `BallFloat::pown`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:815
msgid "`square` returns $\\{\\xi^2\\}$ and `pown` returns $\\{\\xi^n\\}$ for an integer exponent $n$."
msgstr "`square` 返回 $\\{\\xi^2\\}$，`pown` 对整数指数 $n$ 返回 $\\{\\xi^n\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:823
msgid "Unlike `x * x`, these use the same point twice, so `[-1, 2].square()` is $[0, 4]$ (while `x * x` is $[-2, 4]$): `square` is $[\\operatorname{mig}(\\boldsymbol{x})^2, \\operatorname{mag}(\\boldsymbol{x})^2]$. `pown` evaluates the monotone pieces of $\\xi^n$ at the endpoints with directed rounding: odd positive powers are increasing; even positive powers decrease then increase, with minimum 0 when $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$; negative powers have a pole at 0. `pown(x, 0)` is $\\{1\\}$ for every non-empty `x`; Empty stays Empty. `pown(x, n)` with $n < 0$ returns Empty for $\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$, a half-unbounded interval when 0 is an endpoint, and for 0 in the interior Entire (odd $n$) or $[\\min(\\underline{x}^n, \\overline{x}^n), +\\infty)$ (even $n$). As a shortcut, $n < -4096$ with 0 in the interior returns Entire even for even $n$; this is a valid but not tight enclosure."
msgstr "与 `x * x` 不同，这些函数两次使用的是同一个点，因此 `[-1, 2].square()` 为 $[0, 4]$（而 `x * x` 为 $[-2, 4]$）：`square` 为 $[\\operatorname{mig}(\\boldsymbol{x})^2, \\operatorname{mag}(\\boldsymbol{x})^2]$。`pown` 以定向舍入在端点处计算 $\\xi^n$ 的各单调分段：奇数正次幂递增；偶数正次幂先减后增，当 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$ 时最小值为 0；负次幂在 0 处有极点。对每个非空的 `x`，`pown(x, 0)` 为 $\\{1\\}$；Empty 仍为 Empty。当 $n < 0$ 时，`pown(x, n)` 对 $\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$ 返回 Empty，当 0 为端点时返回半无界区间，当 0 位于内部时返回 Entire（$n$ 为奇数）或 $[\\min(\\underline{x}^n, \\overline{x}^n), +\\infty)$（$n$ 为偶数）。作为捷径，当 $n < -4096$ 且 0 位于内部时，即使 $n$ 为偶数也返回 Entire；这是一个有效但不紧的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:850
msgid "`fma(x, y, z)` returns an enclosure of $\\{\\xi\\eta + \\zeta\\}$ with a single outward rounding."
msgstr "`fma(x, y, z)` 以单次向外舍入返回 $\\{\\xi\\eta + \\zeta\\}$ 的一个包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:857
msgid "The exact product bounds are computed as for `mul` and added to the endpoints of $\\boldsymbol{z}$ before the final rounding, so the result is never wider than `x * y + z`."
msgstr "精确的乘积界按 `mul` 的方式计算，并在最终舍入之前加到 $\\boldsymbol{z}$ 的端点上，因此结果绝不会比 `x * y + z` 更宽。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:861
msgid "`BallFloat::minimum` and `BallFloat::maximum`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::minimum` 与 `BallFloat::maximum`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:863
msgid "`minimum` and `maximum` return $\\{\\min(\\xi, \\eta)\\}$ and $\\{\\max(\\xi, \\eta)\\}$."
msgstr "`minimum` 和 `maximum` 分别返回 $\\{\\min(\\xi, \\eta)\\}$ 和 $\\{\\max(\\xi, \\eta)\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:871
msgid "`minimum` is $[\\min(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\min(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$ and `maximum` is the analogue with `max`: $\\min$ is increasing in each argument. An Empty operand gives Empty."
msgstr "`minimum` 为 $[\\min(\\underline{x}, \\underline{y}), \\min(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})]$，`maximum` 则是将其中的 min 换成 `max` 的类似形式：$\\min$ 关于每个参数都是递增的。有 Empty 操作数时结果为 Empty。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:875
#: manual/api/ball_float_checked.md:313
#: manual/api/bin_float.md:1392
#: manual/api/bin_float_checked.md:390
#: manual/api/decimal.md:1307
#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:154
#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:442
msgid "Elementary functions"
msgstr "初等函数"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:877
msgid "Each function $f$ returns an interval containing $f(\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f)$, where $D_f$ is the domain of $f$; points of $\\boldsymbol{x}$ outside $D_f$ are ignored and the result is Empty when $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f$ is empty. The result precision is the argument's precision."
msgstr "每个函数 $f$ 返回一个包含 $f(\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f)$ 的区间，其中 $D_f$ 是 $f$ 的定义域；$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 中位于 $D_f$ 之外的点被忽略，当 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f$ 为空时结果为 Empty。结果精度为参数的精度。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:883
msgid "Functions come in two forms. The total form (`exp_interval`, `sin_interval`, …) always returns a valid enclosure; when the certified evaluation exhausts its refinement budget it returns a wider, still valid, interval. The `try_` form (`try_exp_interval`, …) returns `Err(ArithmeticError)` in that case, with a certification-failure detail naming the operation, stage and reason. Except where noted, the `try_` forms evaluate each endpoint with the corresponding `bin_float` `try_*_ctx` function rounded toward $-\\infty$ or $+\\infty$; the total forms either call them or use the certified series of this package. Both forms return the same set on ordinary inputs; their bounds may differ by an ulp."
msgstr "函数有两种形式。全函数形式（`exp_interval`、`sin_interval` 等）总是返回有效的包络；当认证求值耗尽其细化预算时，它返回一个更宽但仍然有效的区间。`try_` 形式（`try_exp_interval` 等）在这种情况下返回 `Err(ArithmeticError)`，并附带指明运算、阶段和原因的认证失败详情。除另有说明外，`try_` 形式使用对应的 `bin_float` `try_*_ctx` 函数，以向 $-\\infty$ 或 $+\\infty$ 舍入的方式对每个端点求值；全函数形式则要么调用这些函数，要么使用本包中的认证级数。在普通输入上两种形式返回相同的集合；它们的界可能相差一个 ulp。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:896
msgid "`sqrt_interval` returns $\\sqrt{\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap [0, +\\infty)}$."
msgstr "`sqrt_interval` 返回 $\\sqrt{\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap [0, +\\infty)}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:902
msgid "The endpoints are the downward and upward square roots at the interval's precision. Empty when $\\overline{x} < 0$. There is no `try_` form: square root never fails."
msgstr "端点是区间精度下向下和向上舍入的平方根。当 $\\overline{x} < 0$ 时为 Empty。没有 `try_` 形式：平方根从不失败。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:908
msgid "These return enclosures of $e^{\\xi}$, $2^{\\xi}$, $10^{\\xi}$ and $e^{\\xi} - 1$."
msgstr "这些函数分别返回 $e^{\\xi}$、$2^{\\xi}$、$10^{\\xi}$ 和 $e^{\\xi} - 1$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:922
msgid "All four are increasing, so the result is $[\\operatorname{RD} f(\\underline{x}), \\operatorname{RU} f(\\overline{x})]$. `exp_interval` uses a certified Taylor series with argument halving and never needs a fallback; for $|\\xi| \\ge 2^{30}$ it returns $[\\text{largest finite}, +\\infty)$ or $[0, \\text{smallest positive}]$, which is valid because $e^{2^{30}}$ exceeds $2^{e_{\\max}+1}$ and $e^{-2^{30}}$ is below the smallest positive `BinFloat` at every precision. `exp2_interval` and `exp10_interval` evaluate $e^{\\xi \\ln b}$ at 96 extra bits and return exact powers for integer endpoints (for `exp2_interval`, exponents $e_{\\min} \\le n \\le e_{\\max}$, where $2^n$ is a normal `BinFloat`; for `exp10_interval`, exponents $0 \\le n \\le 100000$). An integer endpoint outside the exponent range keeps the outward-rounded series enclosure, so `exp2_interval` of $\\{-1073742000\\}$ is $[0, \\text{smallest positive}]$ and of $\\{2^{30}\\}$ is $[\\text{largest finite}, +\\infty)$. The total `expm1_interval` falls back to $[-1, +\\infty)$."
msgstr "四者都是递增的，因此结果为 $[\\operatorname{RD} f(\\underline{x}), \\operatorname{RU} f(\\overline{x})]$。`exp_interval` 使用带参数折半的认证 Taylor 级数，从不需要回退；当 $|\\xi| \\ge 2^{30}$ 时，它返回 $[\\text{largest finite}, +\\infty)$ 或 $[0, \\text{smallest positive}]$，这是有效的，因为在任何精度下 $e^{2^{30}}$ 都超过 $2^{e_{\\max}+1}$，而 $e^{-2^{30}}$ 都低于最小的正 `BinFloat`。`exp2_interval` 和 `exp10_interval` 以多 96 位的精度计算 $e^{\\xi \\ln b}$，并对整数端点返回精确的幂（对 `exp2_interval`，指数需满足 $e_{\\min} \\le n \\le e_{\\max}$，此时 $2^n$ 是正规的 `BinFloat`；对 `exp10_interval`，指数需满足 $0 \\le n \\le 100000$）。超出指数范围的整数端点保留向外舍入的级数包络，因此 `exp2_interval` 作用于 $\\{-1073742000\\}$ 的结果为 $[0, \\text{smallest positive}]$，作用于 $\\{2^{30}\\}$ 的结果为 $[\\text{largest finite}, +\\infty)$。全函数形式的 `expm1_interval` 回退为 $[-1, +\\infty)$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:940
msgid "These return enclosures of $\\ln \\xi$, $\\log_2 \\xi$, $\\log_{10} \\xi$ and $\\ln(1 + \\xi)$ over their domains $(0, \\infty)$ and $(-1, \\infty)$."
msgstr "这些函数分别在其定义域 $(0, \\infty)$ 和 $(-1, \\infty)$ 上返回 $\\ln \\xi$、$\\log_2 \\xi$、$\\log_{10} \\xi$ 和 $\\ln(1 + \\xi)$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:954
msgid "When the interval reaches the domain boundary ($\\underline{x} \\le 0$, or $\\underline{x} \\le -1$ for `log1p`) the lower endpoint is $-\\infty$; when it lies entirely outside the domain ($\\overline{x} \\le 0$, or $\\overline{x} < -1$ for `log1p`) the result is Empty. `log10_interval` returns exact integers at endpoints $10^k$, $0 \\le k \\le 9$. The total `log1p_interval` falls back to Entire."
msgstr "当区间到达定义域边界（$\\underline{x} \\le 0$，对 `log1p` 为 $\\underline{x} \\le -1$）时，下端点为 $-\\infty$；当区间完全位于定义域之外（$\\overline{x} \\le 0$，对 `log1p` 为 $\\overline{x} < -1$）时，结果为 Empty。`log10_interval` 在端点 $10^k$（$0 \\le k \\le 9$）处返回精确整数。全函数形式的 `log1p_interval` 回退为 Entire。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:979
msgid "`BallFloat::pow_interval` and `BallFloat::try_pow_interval`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::pow_interval` 与 `BallFloat::try_pow_interval`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:981
msgid "`pow_interval(x, y)` returns an enclosure of $\\{\\xi^{\\eta} : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}\\}$ over the IEEE 1788 domain of `pow`: $\\xi > 0$, or $\\xi = 0$ and $\\eta > 0$."
msgstr "`pow_interval(x, y)` 在 IEEE 1788 中 `pow` 的定义域（$\\xi > 0$，或 $\\xi = 0$ 且 $\\eta > 0$）上返回 $\\{\\xi^{\\eta} : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}\\}$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:990
msgid "Negative parts of the base are ignored (use `pown` or `rootn` for negative bases). Since $\\xi^\\eta = e^{\\eta \\ln \\xi}$ and $\\eta \\ln \\xi$ is bilinear in $(\\ln \\xi, \\eta)$, the extrema over a box with $\\underline{x} > 0$ are at the four corners. When the base reaches 0, $\\xi^\\eta \\to 0$ for $\\eta > 0$ and $\\to +\\infty$ for $\\eta < 0$, so the result is extended by 0 or $+\\infty$ accordingly. The code also adds the value 1 when the base interval contains 1 or the exponent interval contains 0; it already lies between the corner values, so this changes nothing but is harmless. $0^{\\eta}$ for $\\eta \\le 0$ is excluded, so `pow_interval([0, 0], y)` is Empty when $\\overline{y} \\le 0$. The result precision is the larger operand precision. A corner whose power is representable at the result precision, such as $16^{3/4} = 8$, gives that power exactly. The total form falls back to an evaluation of $e^{\\eta \\ln \\xi}$ at 192 extra bits."
msgstr "底数的负值部分被忽略（负底数请使用 `pown` 或 `rootn`）。由于 $\\xi^\\eta = e^{\\eta \\ln \\xi}$，且 $\\eta \\ln \\xi$ 关于 $(\\ln \\xi, \\eta)$ 是双线性的，在 $\\underline{x} > 0$ 的矩形上极值位于四个角点。当底数到达 0 时，对 $\\eta > 0$ 有 $\\xi^\\eta \\to 0$，对 $\\eta < 0$ 则 $\\to +\\infty$，因此结果相应地扩展到 0 或 $+\\infty$。当底数区间包含 1 或指数区间包含 0 时，代码还会加入值 1；该值本已位于角点值之间，因此这不会改变任何东西，但也无害。$\\eta \\le 0$ 时的 $0^{\\eta}$ 被排除，因此当 $\\overline{y} \\le 0$ 时 `pow_interval([0, 0], y)` 为 Empty。结果精度为操作数中较大的精度。若某个角点的幂在结果精度下可表示（例如 $16^{3/4} = 8$），则精确给出该幂。全函数形式回退为以多 192 位的精度计算 $e^{\\eta \\ln \\xi}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1004
msgid "`BallFloat::rootn` and `BallFloat::try_rootn`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::rootn` 与 `BallFloat::try_rootn`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1006
msgid "`rootn(x, n)` returns an enclosure of the real $n$-th roots $\\{\\xi^{1/n}\\}$: for even $n$ over $\\xi \\ge 0$, for odd $n$ over all reals, and for negative $n$ the reciprocal of the root."
msgstr "`rootn(x, n)` 返回实 $n$ 次方根 $\\{\\xi^{1/n}\\}$ 的包络：$n$ 为偶数时在 $\\xi \\ge 0$ 上，$n$ 为奇数时在全体实数上，$n$ 为负时取方根的倒数。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1015
msgid "`rootn(x, 0)` and `rootn(x, Int min)` are Empty; `try_rootn(x, 0)` is a domain error. `rootn(x, 1)` is `x` and `rootn(x, 2)` is `sqrt_interval`. The total form evaluates other degrees through `pow_interval` with an enclosure of $1/n$, so it may be slightly wider than `try_rootn`; negative degrees are `rootn(x, -n).reciprocal()`. For negative $n$, `try_rootn` returns Entire when an odd root's argument contains 0 (wider than the total form when 0 is an endpoint). Exact roots are returned exactly for every degree, so `try_rootn({8}, -3)` is $\\{1/2\\}$."
msgstr "`rootn(x, 0)` 和 `rootn(x, Int min)` 为 Empty；`try_rootn(x, 0)` 为定义域错误。`rootn(x, 1)` 即 `x`，`rootn(x, 2)` 即 `sqrt_interval`。全函数形式通过 `pow_interval` 并结合 $1/n$ 的包络来计算其他次数，因此可能比 `try_rootn` 稍宽；负次数即 `rootn(x, -n).reciprocal()`。当 $n$ 为负且奇次方根的参数包含 0 时，`try_rootn` 返回 Entire（当 0 为端点时比全函数形式更宽）。对任何次数，精确根都会被精确返回，因此 `try_rootn({8}, -3)` 为 $\\{1/2\\}$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1037
msgid "`BallFloat::hypot` and `BallFloat::try_hypot`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::hypot` 与 `BallFloat::try_hypot`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1039
msgid "`hypot` returns an enclosure of $\\{\\sqrt{\\xi^2 + \\eta^2}\\}$."
msgstr "`hypot` 返回 $\\{\\sqrt{\\xi^2 + \\eta^2}\\}$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1046
msgid "The function is increasing in $|\\xi|$ and $|\\eta|$, so the result is $[\\operatorname{RD}\\operatorname{hypot}(\\operatorname{mig}\\boldsymbol{x}, \\operatorname{mig}\\boldsymbol{y}), \\operatorname{RU}\\operatorname{hypot}(\\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{x}, \\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{y})]$, evaluated on the endpoints of `abs(x)` and `abs(y)`. The total form falls back to `sqrt_interval(square(x) + square(y))`."
msgstr "该函数关于 $|\\xi|$ 和 $|\\eta|$ 递增，因此结果为 $[\\operatorname{RD}\\operatorname{hypot}(\\operatorname{mig}\\boldsymbol{x}, \\operatorname{mig}\\boldsymbol{y}), \\operatorname{RU}\\operatorname{hypot}(\\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{x}, \\operatorname{mag}\\boldsymbol{y})]$，在 `abs(x)` 与 `abs(y)` 的端点处求值。全函数形式回退为 `sqrt_interval(square(x) + square(y))`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1054
msgid "These return enclosures of $\\sin$, $\\cos$ and $\\tan$ over the interval (in radians)."
msgstr "这些函数返回 $\\sin$、$\\cos$ 和 $\\tan$ 在区间上（以弧度计）的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1066
msgid "Both forms reduce each endpoint by a certified enclosure of $\\pi/2$ and evaluate certified Taylor series. A critical point $k\\pi/2$ inside the interval contributes the extremum $\\pm 1$ of `sin`/`cos` (`sin` reaches $+1$ at $k \\equiv 1$ and $-1$ at $k \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4$, `cos` reaches $+1$ at $k \\equiv 0$ and $-1$ at $k \\equiv 2$); for `tan` an odd multiple of $\\pi/2$ inside the interval (a pole) makes the result Entire. The set of candidate indices $k$ is computed from the enclosure of $\\pi$ and can only be too large, which widens but never invalidates the result. Unbounded arguments give $[-1, 1]$ (Entire for `tan`). When the larger endpoint magnitude is at least $2^{\\max(65536,\\, 4p) + 1}$, the total forms return $[-1, 1]$ (Entire) without evaluating and the `try_` forms return a resource-limit error; the total forms use the same fallback when the certification budget (12 work precisions) is exhausted."
msgstr "两种形式都用 $\\pi/2$ 的认证包络对每个端点进行约简，并计算认证 Taylor 级数。区间内的临界点 $k\\pi/2$ 贡献 `sin`/`cos` 的极值 $\\pm 1$（`sin` 在 $k \\equiv 1$ 处取 $+1$，在 $k \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4$ 处取 $-1$；`cos` 在 $k \\equiv 0$ 处取 $+1$，在 $k \\equiv 2$ 处取 $-1$）；对于 `tan`，区间内若有 $\\pi/2$ 的奇数倍（极点），结果为 Entire。候选下标 $k$ 的集合由 $\\pi$ 的包络计算得出，只可能偏大，这只会使结果变宽而绝不会使其失效。无界参数给出 $[-1, 1]$（对 `tan` 为 Entire）。当较大端点的绝对值至少为 $2^{\\max(65536,\\, 4p) + 1}$ 时，全函数形式不经求值直接返回 $[-1, 1]$（Entire），`try_` 形式返回资源限制错误；当认证预算（12 个工作精度）耗尽时，全函数形式也使用同样的回退。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1082
msgid "These return enclosures of $\\sin \\pi\\xi$, $\\cos \\pi\\xi$ and $\\tan \\pi\\xi$."
msgstr "这些函数返回 $\\sin \\pi\\xi$、$\\cos \\pi\\xi$ 和 $\\tan \\pi\\xi$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1093
msgid "Here the critical points are the exact half-integers $k/2$, located from the dyadic endpoints without approximating $\\pi$. `tanpi_interval` returns a half-unbounded interval when a pole is exactly an endpoint and no other pole lies in the interval (for example $[1/2, 1]$ gives $(-\\infty, 0]$, whose upper endpoint is $\\tan \\pi = -0$), Empty for the singleton of a pole, and Entire when a pole lies inside. Unbounded arguments and fallbacks give $[-1, 1]$ (Entire for `tanpi`)."
msgstr "此处临界点是精确的半整数 $k/2$，由二进有理数端点直接定位，无需近似 $\\pi$。当极点恰好是端点且区间内没有其他极点时，`tanpi_interval` 返回半无界区间（例如 $[1/2, 1]$ 给出 $(-\\infty, 0]$，其上端点为 $\\tan \\pi = -0$）；对极点的单点集返回 Empty；当极点位于区间内部时返回 Entire。无界参数和回退给出 $[-1, 1]$（对 `tanpi` 为 Entire）。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1116
msgid "These return enclosures of $\\arcsin$, $\\arccos$ (over $[-1, 1]$) and $\\arctan$."
msgstr "这些函数返回 $\\arcsin$、$\\arccos$（在 $[-1, 1]$ 上）和 $\\arctan$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1128
msgid "`asin` and `atan` are increasing and `acos` is decreasing, so only endpoints are evaluated. The total `atan_interval` uses a certified series with a Machin-formula enclosure of $\\pi$ and falls back to $[0, \\pi/2]$ or $[-\\pi/2, 0]$ for an endpoint whose budget runs out; `asin` is computed as $\\arctan(\\xi/\\sqrt{1 - \\xi^2})$ and `acos` as $\\pi/2 - \\arcsin \\xi$, at 64 extra bits. `atan` of an infinite endpoint is $\\pm\\pi/2$."
msgstr "`asin` 和 `atan` 递增，`acos` 递减，因此只需对端点求值。全函数形式的 `atan_interval` 使用认证级数，并以 Machin 公式得到 $\\pi$ 的包络；对于预算耗尽的端点，它回退为 $[0, \\pi/2]$ 或 $[-\\pi/2, 0]$。`asin` 按 $\\arctan(\\xi/\\sqrt{1 - \\xi^2})$ 计算，`acos` 按 $\\pi/2 - \\arcsin \\xi$ 计算，均多用 64 位精度。无穷端点的 `atan` 为 $\\pm\\pi/2$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1135
msgid "`BallFloat::atan2_interval` and `BallFloat::try_atan2_interval`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::atan2_interval` 与 `BallFloat::try_atan2_interval`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1137
msgid ""
"`y.atan2_interval(x)` returns an enclosure of the angles $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\eta, \\xi) \\in (-\\pi, \\pi]$ of the points $(\\xi, \\eta) \\n"
"e (0, 0)$ of the box $\\boldsymbol{x} \\times \\boldsymbol{y}$."
msgstr ""
"`y.atan2_interval(x)` 返回矩形 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\times \\boldsymbol{y}$ 中各点 $(\\xi, \\eta) \\n"
"e (0, 0)$ 的辐角 $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\eta, \\xi) \\in (-\\pi, \\pi]$ 的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1146
msgid "The receiver is the ordinate. The result is the hull of the angles at the four corners and at the points where the box meets the axes. When the box crosses the branch cut ($\\underline{x} < 0$ and $\\underline{y} < 0 \\le \\overline{y}$) the result is $[-\\pi, \\pi]$. The box $\\{(0, 0)\\}$ gives Empty. The total form falls back to $[-\\pi, \\pi]$."
msgstr "接收者是纵坐标。结果是四个角点以及矩形与坐标轴交点处的辐角的包。当矩形跨越分支切割线（$\\underline{x} < 0$ 且 $\\underline{y} < 0 \\le \\overline{y}$）时，结果为 $[-\\pi, \\pi]$。矩形 $\\{(0, 0)\\}$ 给出 Empty。全函数形式回退为 $[-\\pi, \\pi]$。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1154
msgid "These return enclosures of the hyperbolic functions and their inverses over their domains ($[1, \\infty)$ for `acosh`, $(-1, 1)$ for `atanh`)."
msgstr "这些函数在各自定义域上（`acosh` 为 $[1, \\infty)$，`atanh` 为 $(-1, 1)$）返回双曲函数及其反函数的包络。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1172
msgid "`cosh` has its minimum 1 at 0; the others are monotone. The total forms evaluate the defining formulas ($(e^\\xi - e^{-\\xi})/2$, $\\ln(\\xi + \\sqrt{\\xi^2 + 1})$, $\\tfrac12 \\ln\\frac{1+\\xi}{1-\\xi}$, …) in interval arithmetic at $w = p + 192$ bits at each endpoint, so they never fail; `tanh_interval` is clipped to $[-1, 1]$. `atanh` of an interval reaching $\\pm 1$ is unbounded on that side. The `try_` forms use the certified `bin_float` kernels instead."
msgstr "`cosh` 在 0 处取最小值 1；其余函数都是单调的。全函数形式在每个端点处以 $w = p + 192$ 位的精度用区间算术计算定义公式（$(e^\\xi - e^{-\\xi})/2$、$\\ln(\\xi + \\sqrt{\\xi^2 + 1})$、$\\tfrac12 \\ln\\frac{1+\\xi}{1-\\xi}$ 等），因此从不失败；`tanh_interval` 被截断到 $[-1, 1]$。若区间到达 $\\pm 1$，其 `atanh` 在该侧无界。`try_` 形式则使用经认证的 `bin_float` 内核。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1180
msgid "The defining formulas of `sinh`, `tanh`, `asinh` and `atanh` cancel near 0: their absolute error is about $2^{-w}$, so for $|\\xi|$ below roughly $2^{-190}$ the total forms are valid but far from tight. At 53 bits, `sinh_interval` of $\\{2^{-300}\\}$ is $[0, 3 \\cdot 2^{-246}]$ while `try_sinh_interval` returns the two-ulp interval $[2^{-300}, (1 + 2^{-52})\\,2^{-300}]$. Use the `try_` forms for tiny arguments."
msgstr "`sinh`、`tanh`、`asinh` 和 `atanh` 的定义公式在 0 附近会发生抵消：其绝对误差约为 $2^{-w}$，因此当 $|\\xi|$ 低于大约 $2^{-190}$ 时，全函数形式虽然有效但远不紧。在 53 位下，$\\{2^{-300}\\}$ 的 `sinh_interval` 为 $[0, 3 \\cdot 2^{-246}]$，而 `try_sinh_interval` 返回两个 ulp 宽的区间 $[2^{-300}, (1 + 2^{-52})\\,2^{-300}]$。对于极小的参数，请使用 `try_` 形式。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1200
msgid "Contexts and flags"
msgstr "上下文与标志"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1202
msgid "`BallContext::new` and `BallContext::try_new`"
msgstr "`BallContext::new` 与 `BallContext::try_new`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1204
msgid "`BallContext::new` builds a context from a precision and an exponent range."
msgstr "`BallContext::new` 由精度和指数范围构建上下文。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1211
msgid "The defaults are those of binary64: precision 53, $e_{\\min} = -1022$, $e_{\\max} = 1023$. A precision below 1 or $e_{\\min} > e_{\\max}$ aborts `new` and is a domain error for `try_new`."
msgstr "默认值为 binary64 的参数：精度 53，$e_{\\min} = -1022$，$e_{\\max} = 1023$。精度小于 1 或 $e_{\\min} > e_{\\max}$ 会使 `new` 中止，对 `try_new` 则是定义域错误。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1215
msgid "`BallContext::binary32` and `BallContext::binary64`"
msgstr "`BallContext::binary32` 与 `BallContext::binary64`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1217
msgid "These return the contexts of the IEEE 754 binary32 ($p = 24$, $[-126, 127]$) and binary64 ($p = 53$, $[-1022, 1023]$) formats."
msgstr "它们返回 IEEE 754 binary32（$p = 24$，$[-126, 127]$）与 binary64（$p = 53$，$[-1022, 1023]$）格式的上下文。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1227
msgid "These return the parameters of a context."
msgstr "它们返回上下文的参数。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1237
msgid "`BallFlags::new` returns the flags with nothing raised; `combine` is their union; the accessors read the fields."
msgstr "`BallFlags::new` 返回未触发任何条件的标志；`combine` 求二者的并；访问器读取各字段。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1250
msgid "`apply_ctx` rounds an interval outward into a context and reports the flags."
msgstr "`apply_ctx` 将区间向外舍入到上下文中并报告标志。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1256
msgid "Each finite nonzero endpoint is rounded outward to the context precision. An endpoint whose rounded exponent exceeds $e_{\\max}$ overflows: it becomes $\\mp\\infty$ if it is a negative lower or a positive upper endpoint, and the largest finite value of the right sign otherwise (a positive lower endpoint becomes the largest finite value, which is still below it). An endpoint below the normal range is then rounded outward on the subnormal grid $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}\\mathbb{Z}$, so a tiny positive upper endpoint becomes the smallest subnormal rather than 0. Rounding twice in the same direction equals rounding once onto the coarser grid, so the endpoints are the directed roundings of the stored ones. Zeros and infinities are kept. Empty gives Empty with no flags. The result has the context precision."
msgstr "每个有限非零端点都向外舍入到上下文精度。舍入后指数超过 $e_{\\max}$ 的端点发生上溢：若它是负的下端点或正的上端点，则变为 $\\mp\\infty$；否则变为相应符号的最大有限值（正的下端点变为最大有限值，仍低于原值）。随后，低于正规范围的端点在次正规网格 $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}\\mathbb{Z}$ 上向外舍入，因此极小的正上端点会变为最小次正规数而不是 0。同一方向的两次舍入等于一次舍入到较粗的网格上，因此所得端点就是所存储端点的定向舍入。零和无穷保持不变。Empty 给出 Empty 且不设任何标志。结果具有上下文精度。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1268
msgid "`underflow` follows IEEE 754 with tininess detected after rounding: it is raised when an endpoint is inexact and its rounding to $p$ bits with an unbounded exponent range lies below $2^{e_{\\min}}$, whichever of the two steps lost the bits. With $p = 4$ and $e_{\\min} = -2$, the lower endpoint $2^{-3}(1 + 2^{-10})$ becomes $2^{-3}$, which is already on the subnormal grid, and raises both `inexact` and `underflow`. An exact tiny endpoint raises nothing."
msgstr "`underflow` 遵循 IEEE 754，并在舍入之后检测微小性：当端点不精确，且其在指数范围无界时舍入到 $p$ 位的结果低于 $2^{e_{\\min}}$ 时引发，无论丢失位数的是两步中的哪一步。在 $p = 4$、$e_{\\min} = -2$ 时，下端点 $2^{-3}(1 + 2^{-10})$ 变为 $2^{-3}$，它已在次正规网格上，并同时引发 `inexact` 和 `underflow`。精确的微小端点不引发任何标志。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1278
msgid "These compute the operation and then apply the context."
msgstr "它们先计算运算，再应用上下文。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1287
msgid "`x.add_ctx(y, ctx)` is `(x + y).apply_ctx(ctx)`. When the operands' precision is at least the context precision, the double rounding gives the same endpoints as a single outward rounding into the context (see the [design page](../design/ball_float.md#contexts-and-double-rounding))."
msgstr "`x.add_ctx(y, ctx)` 即 `(x + y).apply_ctx(ctx)`。当操作数的精度不低于上下文精度时，这种两次舍入得到的端点与一次向外舍入到上下文所得的端点相同（参见[设计文档](../design/ball_float.md#contexts-and-double-rounding)）。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1292
msgid "`BallFloat::exp_ctx` and `BallFloat::ln_ctx`"
msgstr "`BallFloat::exp_ctx` 与 `BallFloat::ln_ctx`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1294
msgid "`exp_ctx` and `ln_ctx` evaluate `exp_interval` and `ln_interval` at 32 bits more than the context precision and then apply the context."
msgstr "`exp_ctx` 和 `ln_ctx` 以比上下文精度多 32 位的精度计算 `exp_interval` 和 `ln_interval`，然后应用上下文。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1304
msgid "`midpoint_ctx` is the IEEE 1788 `mid` operation with the context as the result format."
msgstr "`midpoint_ctx` 是以上下文为结果格式的 IEEE 1788 `mid` 运算。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1311
msgid "Following IEEE 1788-2015 §12.12.8, Empty gives NaN, Entire gives $+0$, an interval unbounded only above gives the largest finite value of the context, $(2 - 2^{1-p})\\,2^{e_{\\max}}$, and one unbounded only below gives its negative; none of these raises a flag. A bounded interval gives its exact center rounded once to nearest (ties to even) onto the context's grid, including the subnormal grid $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}\\mathbb{Z}$, so with $p = 4$, $e_{\\min} = -2$ the center $2^{-6} + 2^{-20}$ gives $2^{-5}$. A zero center gives $+0$. `inexact` is set when the result differs from the center and `underflow` when it is also tiny, as for `apply_ctx`. A center that rounds beyond $e_{\\max}$ overflows to an infinity of its sign with `overflow` and `inexact`: rounding to nearest maps it to $\\pm\\infty$ in IEEE 754, and IEEE 1788 uses that rounding for the bounded case. Only an interval whose endpoints are themselves outside the context's range can do this."
msgstr "按照 IEEE 1788-2015 §12.12.8，Empty 给出 NaN，Entire 给出 $+0$，仅上方无界的区间给出上下文的最大有限值 $(2 - 2^{1-p})\\,2^{e_{\\max}}$，仅下方无界的区间给出其相反数；这些情形都不引发标志。有界区间给出其精确中心一次性按就近舍入（平局取偶）到上下文网格（包括次正规网格 $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}\\mathbb{Z}$）上的值，因此在 $p = 4$、$e_{\\min} = -2$ 时，中心 $2^{-6} + 2^{-20}$ 给出 $2^{-5}$。零中心给出 $+0$。结果与中心不同时设置 `inexact`，若同时为微小值则设置 `underflow`，与 `apply_ctx` 相同。舍入后超出 $e_{\\max}$ 的中心溢出为同号的无穷，并设置 `overflow` 和 `inexact`：在 IEEE 754 中就近舍入将其映射为 $\\pm\\infty$，而 IEEE 1788 在有界情形下使用的正是这种舍入。只有端点本身就超出上下文范围的区间才会出现这种情况。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1341
msgid "Decorated intervals"
msgstr "装饰区间"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1343
msgid "A decorated operation computes the bare result and the decoration $d = \\min(d_1, \\dots, d_k, d_f)$, where $d_i$ are the operand decorations and $d_f$ is the decoration of the operation on these operands (`Com` when the function is defined and continuous on the whole input box, `Trv` when the input leaves the domain, as listed below). The minimum is then made canonical (Empty → `Trv`, unbounded with `Com` → `Dac`). Any NaI operand gives NaI."
msgstr "装饰运算计算裸结果以及装饰 $d = \\min(d_1, \\dots, d_k, d_f)$，其中 $d_i$ 是操作数的装饰，$d_f$ 是该运算在这些操作数上的装饰（当函数在整个输入矩形上有定义且连续时为 `Com`，当输入超出定义域时为 `Trv`，如下文所列）。随后将该最小值规范化（Empty → `Trv`，无界且为 `Com` → `Dac`）。任何 NaI 操作数都给出 NaI。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1352
msgid "`BallFloatDecorated::new` decorates a bare interval."
msgstr "`BallFloatDecorated::new` 为裸区间添加装饰。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1358
msgid "The default decoration is `Com`. The decoration is made canonical, and `Ill` is replaced by `Trv`: `new` never builds NaI. `new(whole())` is therefore decorated `Dac` and `new(empty())` is decorated `Trv`, as in IEEE 1788 `newDec`."
msgstr "默认装饰为 `Com`。装饰会被规范化，且 `Ill` 会被替换为 `Trv`：`new` 从不构建 NaI。因此，与 IEEE 1788 的 `newDec` 一样，`new(whole())` 的装饰为 `Dac`，`new(empty())` 的装饰为 `Trv`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1363
msgid "`BallFloatDecorated::nai` and `BallFloatDecorated::is_nai`"
msgstr "`BallFloatDecorated::nai` 与 `BallFloatDecorated::is_nai`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1365
msgid "`nai` returns NaI, the result of an invalid decorated construction; `is_nai` tests for it."
msgstr "`nai` 返回 NaI，即无效装饰构造的结果；`is_nai` 检测它。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1373
msgid "NaI has decoration `Ill` and an Empty interval (default precision 53), but it is not Empty: `is_empty` is false for NaI."
msgstr "NaI 的装饰为 `Ill`，区间为 Empty（默认精度 53），但它不是 Empty：对 NaI，`is_empty` 为假。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1376
msgid "`BallFloatDecorated::interval` and `BallFloatDecorated::decoration`"
msgstr "`BallFloatDecorated::interval` 与 `BallFloatDecorated::decoration`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1378
msgid "These return the bare interval and the decoration."
msgstr "它们返回裸区间和装饰。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1387
msgid "These predicates apply the bare predicate to the interval and return false for NaI."
msgstr "这些谓词将相应的裸谓词作用于区间，对 NaI 返回假。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1400
msgid "These relations apply the bare relation to the intervals and return false when an operand is NaI."
msgstr "这些关系将相应的裸关系作用于区间，当有操作数为 NaI 时返回假。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1415
msgid "`overlap_state` returns `Undefined` when an operand is NaI."
msgstr "当有操作数为 NaI 时，`overlap_state` 返回 `Undefined`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1419
msgid "These apply the bare operation and always lower the decoration to `Trv` (set operations are not point functions, so no property of a function can be claimed for their results)."
msgstr "这些函数应用裸运算，并总是将装饰降为 `Trv`（集合运算不是逐点函数，因此无法对其结果断言函数的任何性质）。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1432
msgid "The arithmetic operations apply the bare operation; their operation decoration is `Com` except where the table says otherwise."
msgstr "算术运算应用裸运算；除表中另有说明外，其运算装饰为 `Com`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1451
#: manual/design/bin_float_checked.md:122
#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:119
msgid "Operation"
msgstr "操作"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1451
msgid "Operation decoration"
msgstr "运算装饰"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1453
msgid "`Trv` when the divisor contains 0"
msgstr "除数包含 0 时为 `Trv`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1454
msgid "`Trv` when $n < 0$ and $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$"
msgstr "当 $n < 0$ 且 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$ 时为 `Trv`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1455
msgid "identity (IEEE 1788 `pos`)"
msgstr "恒等（IEEE 1788 `pos`）"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1456
msgid "others"
msgstr "其他"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1460
msgid "The decorated elementary functions apply the bare total form (there are no decorated `try_` forms) and lower the decoration when the input leaves the domain of the function, as listed in the table at the end of this group."
msgstr "装饰初等函数应用裸的全函数形式（没有装饰版的 `try_` 形式），并在输入超出函数定义域时降低装饰，具体见本组末尾的表格。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1464
msgid "These are the decorated square root, exponentials, logarithms, powers and `hypot`."
msgstr "这些是装饰版的平方根、指数函数、对数函数、幂函数以及 `hypot`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1484
msgid "These are the decorated trigonometric functions and their inverses."
msgstr "这些是装饰版的三角函数及其反函数。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1501
msgid "These are the decorated hyperbolic functions and their inverses."
msgstr "这些是装饰版的双曲函数及其反函数。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1512
#: manual/api/decimal.md:1490
#: manual/numeric_semantics.md:136
msgid "Function"
msgstr "函数"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1512
msgid "Operation decoration `Trv` when"
msgstr "运算装饰为 `Trv` 的条件"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1514
msgid "$\\underline{x} < 0$ (or the input is Empty)"
msgstr "$\\underline{x} < 0$（或输入为 Empty）"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1519
msgid "$\\underline{x} \\le -1$ or $\\overline{x} \\ge 1$"
msgstr "$\\underline{x} \\le -1$ 或 $\\overline{x} \\ge 1$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1520
msgid "$n = 0$, or $n$ even and $\\underline{x} < 0$, or $n < 0$ and $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$"
msgstr "$n = 0$，或 $n$ 为偶数且 $\\underline{x} < 0$，或 $n < 0$ 且 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1521
msgid "$\\underline{x} < 0$, or $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$ and $\\underline{y} \\le 0$, or the result is Empty"
msgstr "$\\underline{x} < 0$，或 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}$ 且 $\\underline{y} \\le 0$，或结果为 Empty"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1522
msgid "the result is Entire (a pole may lie inside)"
msgstr "结果为 Entire（内部可能有极点）"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1523
msgid "the result is unbounded (a pole lies in the argument, possibly at an endpoint)"
msgstr "结果无界（参数中含有极点，可能位于端点）"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1524
msgid "both operands contain 0"
msgstr "两个操作数都包含 0"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1526
msgid "All other functions have operation decoration `Com`. For `y.atan2_interval(x)` the decoration is `Def` when the box crosses the branch cut ($\\underline{x} < 0$, $\\underline{y} < 0 \\le \\overline{y}$: the restriction jumps from $-\\pi$ to $\\pi$) and `Dac` when it touches the cut from above ($\\overline{x} < 0$, $\\underline{y} = 0$: the restriction is continuous, but `atan2` itself is not continuous at those points)."
msgstr "其他所有函数的运算装饰均为 `Com`。对于 `y.atan2_interval(x)`，当矩形跨越分支切割线（$\\underline{x} < 0$，$\\underline{y} < 0 \\le \\overline{y}$：限制函数从 $-\\pi$ 跳到 $\\pi$）时装饰为 `Def`，当它从上方触及切割线（$\\overline{x} < 0$，$\\underline{y} = 0$：限制函数连续，但 `atan2` 本身在这些点不连续）时装饰为 `Dac`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1535
msgid "`apply_ctx` applies `BallFloat::apply_ctx` to the interval and keeps the decoration (made canonical again, so an overflowed `Com` becomes `Dac`)."
msgstr "`apply_ctx` 将 `BallFloat::apply_ctx` 应用于区间并保留装饰（会再次规范化，因此发生上溢的 `Com` 变为 `Dac`）。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1542
msgid "NaI stays NaI, with the context precision."
msgstr "NaI 仍为 NaI，并带上上下文精度。"

