#: manual/design/bin_float.md:90
msgid "A `BinaryContext` is exactly this triple plus a rounding direction and a tininess rule. Its $e_{\\min}$ and $e_{\\max}$ are leading-bit exponents, so a normal number has $e_{\\min} \\le \\operatorname{top}(x) \\le e_{\\max}$, and the grid below $2^{e_{\\min}}$ has the fixed quantum"
msgstr "`BinaryContext` 恰好就是这个三元组，再加上舍入方向和微小性规则。其 $e_{\\min}$ 和 $e_{\\max}$ 是最高位指数，因此正规数满足 $e_{\\min} \\le \\operatorname{top}(x) \\le e_{\\max}$，而 $2^{e_{\\min}}$ 以下的网格具有固定的量子"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:99
msgid "the smallest positive subnormal. Missing bounds are replaced by the implementation range $\\pm(2^{30}-1)$, which is large enough that every exponent arithmetic step fits a 64-bit intermediate and every stored exponent an `Int`; `binary_precision_max` $= 2^{28}$ keeps $e_{\\min} - p + 1$ in range too."
msgstr "即最小的正次正规数。缺失的界由实现范围 $\\pm(2^{30}-1)$ 代替，该范围足够大，使每一步指数运算都能放入 64 位中间量，每个存储的指数都能放入 `Int`；`binary_precision_max` $= 2^{28}$ 也使 $e_{\\min} - p + 1$ 保持在范围内。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:105
#: manual/numeric_semantics.md:107
msgid "Rounding functions"
msgstr "舍入函数"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:107
msgid "For $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ let $x^- = \\max\\{y \\in F : y \\le x\\}$ and $x^+ = \\min\\{y \\in F : y \\ge x\\}$, extending $F$ by $\\pm\\infty$ beyond $\\pm\\Omega$ for the moment. The six rounding directions of `BinaryRoundingMode` are the maps $\\mathbb{R} \\to F \\cup \\{\\pm\\infty\\}$"
msgstr "对于 $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$，令 $x^- = \\max\\{y \\in F : y \\le x\\}$ 和 $x^+ = \\min\\{y \\in F : y \\ge x\\}$，暂且将 $F$ 在 $\\pm\\Omega$ 之外以 $\\pm\\infty$ 延拓。`BinaryRoundingMode` 的六种舍入方向是映射 $\\mathbb{R} \\to F \\cup \\{\\pm\\infty\\}$"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:121
msgid "where RA (`RoundAwayFromZero`) is not an IEEE attribute but the GDA \"round-up\" mode that `@lf_arith.RoundingMode` shares with the decimal cores. Two properties of every $\\circ$ above carry most of the proofs on this page:"
msgstr "其中 RA（`RoundAwayFromZero`）不是 IEEE 属性，而是 `@lf_arith.RoundingMode` 与十进制核心共用的 GDA \"round-up\" 模式。上述每个 $\\circ$ 的两条性质支撑了本页的大部分证明："

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:129
msgid "(R1) holds because $x^- = x^+ = x$ on $F$. (R2) holds because each $\\circ(x)$ is one of the two neighbours of $x$ chosen by a rule that only moves from $x^-$ to $x^+$ as $x$ increases through a cell $[x^-, x^+]$."
msgstr "(R1) 成立，因为在 $F$ 上 $x^- = x^+ = x$。(R2) 成立，因为每个 $\\circ(x)$ 都是 $x$ 的两个相邻值之一，其选择规则在 $x$ 穿过单元 $[x^-, x^+]$ 增大时只会从 $x^-$ 移到 $x^+$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:133
msgid "The standard error model"
msgstr "标准误差模型"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:135
msgid "Let $u = 2^{-p}$ be the unit roundoff. Take $x$ with $2^{t} \\le |x| < 2^{t+1}$, $t \\ge e_{\\min}$ (the normal range) and $|x|$ below the overflow threshold of the rounding direction (otherwise the result is an infinity and no relative bound holds). The points of $F$ in that binade are spaced $2^{t-p+1}$ apart, and $2^{t+1}$ belongs to $F$ or is the overflow point, so"
msgstr "设 $u = 2^{-p}$ 为单位舍入误差。取满足 $2^{t} \\le |x| < 2^{t+1}$、$t \\ge e_{\\min}$（正规范围）且 $|x|$ 低于该舍入方向上溢阈值的 $x$（否则结果为无穷，不存在相对误差界）。$F$ 在该二进制数量级区间内的点间距为 $2^{t-p+1}$，而 $2^{t+1}$ 属于 $F$ 或者就是上溢点，因此"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:149
msgid "where RN is RNE or RNA. Writing $\\circ(x) = x(1 + \\delta)$ gives the standard model"
msgstr "其中 RN 为 RNE 或 RNA。记 $\\circ(x) = x(1 + \\delta)$，便得到标准模型"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:156
msgid "The nearest bound sharpens to $|\\delta| \\le u/(1+u)$ by dividing by $|\\circ(x)|$ instead of $|x|$.[^higham] Below $2^{e_{\\min}}$ the spacing is the constant $\\eta$, so the error is absolute: $|\\operatorname{RN}(x) - x| \\le \\eta/2$ and $|\\operatorname{RD}(x) - x| < \\eta$. Both regimes together give the model with an underflow term,"
msgstr "将除以 $|x|$ 改为除以 $|\\circ(x)|$，就近舍入的界可加强为 $|\\delta| \\le u/(1+u)$。[^higham] 在 $2^{e_{\\min}}$ 以下，间距为常数 $\\eta$，因此误差是绝对的：$|\\operatorname{RN}(x) - x| \\le \\eta/2$ 且 $|\\operatorname{RD}(x) - x| < \\eta$。两种区段合在一起，得到带下溢项的模型，"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:166
msgid "for nearest rounding ($2u$ and $\\eta$ for directed rounding). Addition and subtraction never need $\\epsilon$: if $a, b \\in F$ then both are integer multiples of $\\eta$, so is $a \\pm b$, and a multiple of $\\eta$ below $2^{e_{\\min}}$ lies in $F$. Hence a subnormal sum is exact, which is why gradual underflow keeps $a - b = 0 \\iff a = b$.[^kahan]"
msgstr "适用于就近舍入（对定向舍入为 $2u$ 和 $\\eta$）。加法和减法从不需要 $\\epsilon$：若 $a, b \\in F$，则二者都是 $\\eta$ 的整数倍，$a \\pm b$ 亦然，而 $2^{e_{\\min}}$ 以下的 $\\eta$ 的倍数位于 $F$ 中。因此次正规的和是精确的，这正是渐进下溢能保持 $a - b = 0 \\iff a = b$ 的原因。[^kahan]"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:172
msgid "N. J. Higham, *Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*, 2nd ed., SIAM 2002, §2.2; D. Goldberg, \"What every computer scientist should know about floating-point arithmetic\", *ACM Computing Surveys* 23(1), 1991."
msgstr "N. J. Higham，*Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*，第 2 版，SIAM 2002，§2.2；D. Goldberg，\"What every computer scientist should know about floating-point arithmetic\"，*ACM Computing Surveys* 23(1)，1991。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:177
msgid "J.-M. Muller et al., *Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*, 2nd ed., Birkhäuser 2018, §2.1 and §4.3."
msgstr "J.-M. Muller 等，*Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*，第 2 版，Birkhäuser 2018，§2.1 与 §4.3。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:180
msgid "Correct rounding is a stronger property than the model: the result is the one point $\\circ(f(x))$, not merely some point within $u$. Every value `bin_float` returns is that point, so the model above holds for every operation, including the elementary functions."
msgstr "正确舍入是比该模型更强的性质：结果是唯一的那个点 $\\circ(f(x))$，而不仅仅是 $u$ 范围内的某个点。`bin_float` 返回的每个值都是这个点，因此上述模型对每个运算都成立，包括初等函数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:187
msgid "Round once from exact data"
msgstr "由精确数据一次舍入"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:189
msgid "**Problem.** A result must equal $\\circ(r)$ for the exact real $r$, but $r$ may need far more bits than $p$ (a product of two $p$-bit numbers has $2p$), or infinitely many (a quotient, a square root, $e^x$)."
msgstr "**问题。** 结果必须等于精确实数 $r$ 的 $\\circ(r)$，但 $r$ 可能需要远多于 $p$ 的位数（两个 $p$ 位数的乘积有 $2p$ 位），甚至无穷多位（商、平方根、$e^x$）。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:193
msgid "**Options.** Compute in a wider format and round again, as hardware without FMA does; or keep a fixed number of guard bits; or decide the rounding from exact information."
msgstr "**可选方案。** 像不带 FMA 的硬件那样在更宽的格式中计算后再舍入一次；或保留固定数量的保护位；或依据精确信息决定舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:197
msgid "**Choice.** Every operation computes an exact description of $r$ and calls one finalizer. For dyadic results (sum, difference, product, `fma`, `scaleb`, `remainder`, conversion) the description is the exact integer magnitude $m$ and exponent $e$ with $r = \\pm m 2^{e}$. The finalizer picks the shift"
msgstr "**选择。** 每个运算都计算 $r$ 的精确描述，并调用一个终结器。对于二进有理结果（和、差、积、`fma`、`scaleb`、`remainder`、转换），该描述是精确的整数绝对值 $m$ 和指数 $e$，满足 $r = \\pm m 2^{e}$。终结器选取移位量"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:207
msgid "the larger of the precision shift and the shift onto the subnormal grid, and splits $m 2^{-\\sigma} = q + f$ with $q = \\lfloor m 2^{-\\sigma} \\rfloor$ and $0 \\le f < 1$ into three items of data:"
msgstr "即精度移位与移到次正规网格的移位二者中较大者，并以 $q = \\lfloor m 2^{-\\sigma} \\rfloor$ 和 $0 \\le f < 1$ 将 $m 2^{-\\sigma} = q + f$ 拆分为三项数据："

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:215
msgid "These are the classical round and sticky bits, read from the coefficient by `test_bit` and `ctz` without building any shifted copy. They determine every rounding direction: with $q_0$ the last bit of $q$,"
msgstr "这就是经典的舍入位和粘滞位，由 `test_bit` 和 `ctz` 直接从系数中读出，无需构造任何移位后的副本。它们决定了每种舍入方向：记 $q_0$ 为 $q$ 的最低位，"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:219
msgid "Direction"
msgstr "方向"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:219
msgid "increment $q$ when"
msgstr "当以下条件成立时递增 $q$"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:221
msgid "RNE"
msgstr "RNE"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:222
msgid "RNA"
msgstr "RNA"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:223
msgid "RZ"
msgstr "RZ"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:223
#: manual/design/decimal.md:168
msgid "never"
msgstr "从不"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:224
msgid "RU"
msgstr "RU"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:225
msgid "RD"
msgstr "RD"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:226
msgid "RA"
msgstr "RA"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:228
msgid ""
"*Derivation.* $f > \\frac12 \\iff g \\wedge t$, $f = \\frac12 \\iff g \\wedge \\n"
"eg t$, and $f > 0 \\iff g \\vee t$. RNE rounds the magnitude up when $f > \\frac12$, or when $f = \\frac12$ and $q$ is odd; that is $(g \\wedge t) \\vee (g \\wedge \\n"
"eg t \\wedge q_0) = g \\wedge (t \\vee q_0)$. The directed rows round the magnitude up exactly when $f > 0$ and the direction points away from zero for the sign $s$. Inexactness is $g \\vee t$."
msgstr ""
"*推导。* $f > \\frac12 \\iff g \\wedge t$、$f = \\frac12 \\iff g \\wedge \\n"
"eg t$ 以及 $f > 0 \\iff g \\vee t$。RNE 在 $f > \\frac12$ 时，或在 $f = \\frac12$ 且 $q$ 为奇数时将绝对值向上舍入；即 $(g \\wedge t) \\vee (g \\wedge \\n"
"eg t \\wedge q_0) = g \\wedge (t \\vee q_0)$。定向舍入各行恰在 $f > 0$ 且舍入方向对符号 $s$ 而言是远离零时将绝对值向上舍入。不精确性即 $g \\vee t$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:235
msgid "**Why.** Because $\\sigma$ already includes the subnormal shift, a tiny result is rounded once, directly from $m$, to the grid $\\eta \\mathbb{Z}$. Rounding first to $p$ bits and then to the subnormal grid would be a double rounding: a value just above a midpoint of the coarse grid can be pushed onto that midpoint by the first rounding and then rounded the wrong way by the second. A carry out of $q$ (when $q + 1 = 2^p$) only raises $\\operatorname{top}$ by one; the result is re-normalized and the overflow test below is applied to the rounded value."
msgstr "**原因。** 由于 $\\sigma$ 已包含次正规移位，极小的结果直接由 $m$ 一次舍入到网格 $\\eta \\mathbb{Z}$。若先舍入到 $p$ 位再舍入到次正规网格，就成了双重舍入：略高于粗网格中点的值可能被第一次舍入推到该中点上，再被第二次舍入朝错误方向舍入。从 $q$ 产生的进位（当 $q + 1 = 2^p$ 时）只会使 $\\operatorname{top}$ 加一；结果随后重新规范化，并对舍入后的值施加下文的上溢检查。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:244
msgid "Division from quotient and remainder"
msgstr "由商和余数实现除法"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:246
msgid "**Problem.** $a/b$ with $a = c_a 2^{e_a}$, $b = c_b 2^{e_b}$ is a rational $N/D \\cdot 2^{e}$ ($N = c_a$, $D = c_b$, $e = e_a - e_b$) whose binary expansion is usually infinite."
msgstr "**问题。** 满足 $a = c_a 2^{e_a}$ 的 $a/b$，$b = c_b 2^{e_b}$ 是有理数 $N/D \\cdot 2^{e}$（$N = c_a$、$D = c_b$、$e = e_a - e_b$），其二进制展开通常是无限的。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:250
msgid "**Choice.** First the exact leading exponent: with $k = \\operatorname{bits}(N) - \\operatorname{bits}(D)$, $\\lfloor \\log_2 (N/D) \\rfloor$ is $k$ if $N \\ge D 2^{k}$ and $k - 1$ otherwise, one integer comparison. That fixes the target exponent $\\tau = \\max(\\operatorname{top} - p + 1,\\ e_{\\min} - p + 1)$, and then one integer division"
msgstr "**选择。** 首先确定精确的最高位指数：设 $k = \\operatorname{bits}(N) - \\operatorname{bits}(D)$，若 $N \\ge D 2^{k}$ 则 $\\lfloor \\log_2 (N/D) \\rfloor$ 为 $k$，否则为 $k - 1$，只需一次整数比较。这确定了目标指数 $\\tau = \\max(\\operatorname{top} - p + 1,\\ e_{\\min} - p + 1)$，随后一次整数除法"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:261
msgid "gives $q$ directly, and the remainder gives the rounding data: $f = r/D$, so"
msgstr "直接给出 $q$，余数则给出舍入数据：$f = r/D$，因此"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:268
msgid "No approximation of $N/D$ is involved; the rounding is decided by the sign of $2r - D$. When $e - \\tau < 0$ the shift is moved to the denominator, and a quotient below one unit is decided by comparing $2N$ with $D 2^{\\tau - e}$ without forming it."
msgstr "不涉及对 $N/D$ 的任何近似；舍入由 $2r - D$ 的符号决定。当 $e - \\tau < 0$ 时，移位被移到分母上；小于一个单位的商通过比较 $2N$ 与 $D 2^{\\tau - e}$ 来判定，而无需构造它。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:273
msgid "Square root from an integer root and a midpoint test"
msgstr "由整数平方根和中点测试实现平方根"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:275
msgid "**Problem.** $\\sqrt{c 2^{e}}$ is irrational unless $c 2^{e}$ is a square."
msgstr "**问题。** 除非 $c 2^{e}$ 是平方数，否则 $\\sqrt{c 2^{e}}$ 是无理数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:277
msgid "**Choice.** The leading exponent is $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x)/2 \\rfloor$ (floor division), which fixes $\\tau$ as above. Write the radicand as $X = c\\, 2^{e - 2\\tau}$, so $\\sqrt{x} = \\sqrt{X}\\, 2^{\\tau}$. An exact integer square root gives $s = \\lfloor \\sqrt{X} \\rfloor$ with remainder $X - s^2$; the root is exact iff the remainder is zero. Otherwise the rounding data come from the midpoint $s + \\frac12$:"
msgstr "**选择。** 最高位指数为 $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x)/2 \\rfloor$（向下取整除法），由此如上确定 $\\tau$。将被开方数写作 $X = c\\, 2^{e - 2\\tau}$，从而 $\\sqrt{x} = \\sqrt{X}\\, 2^{\\tau}$。精确的整数平方根给出 $s = \\lfloor \\sqrt{X} \\rfloor$ 及余数 $X - s^2$；当且仅当余数为零时平方根是精确的。否则，舍入数据来自中点 $s + \\frac12$："

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:288
msgid ""
"an exact comparison of integers (with the power of two moved to the other side when $X$ is fractional). So $g = [4X \\ge (2s+1)^2]$ and $t = \\n"
"eg\\text{exact} \\wedge [4X \\n"
"e (2s+1)^2]$. When $X$ is an integer the right side is odd and the left even, so the root is never exactly a midpoint; this is the classical fact that $\\sqrt{x}$ of a $p$-bit number is never a $(p+1)$-bit midpoint.[^muller-sqrt] The equality branch is still kept, because an operand with more bits than the context precision can make $\\sqrt{X}$ an exact midpoint (for example $\\sqrt{9/4} = 3/2$ rounded to one bit)."
msgstr ""
"这是一次精确的整数比较（当 $X$ 为分数时，将 2 的幂移到另一侧）。因此 $g = [4X \\ge (2s+1)^2]$ 且 $t = \\n"
"eg\\text{exact} \\wedge [4X \\n"
"e (2s+1)^2]$。当 $X$ 为整数时，右边为奇数而左边为偶数，因此平方根从不恰好是中点；这就是经典事实：$p$ 位数的 $\\sqrt{x}$ 从不是 $(p+1)$ 位中点。[^muller-sqrt] 相等分支仍然保留，因为位数多于上下文精度的操作数可能使 $\\sqrt{X}$ 恰好成为中点（例如 $\\sqrt{9/4} = 3/2$ 舍入到一位）。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:298
msgid "Muller et al., *Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*, §5.3 and §7.6."
msgstr "Muller 等，*Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*，§5.3 与 §7.6。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:301
msgid "Exponent range, overflow and underflow"
msgstr "指数范围、上溢与下溢"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:303
msgid "**Overflow** is decided on the rounded value: if the rounded result has $\\operatorname{top} > e_{\\max}$, the operation overflows, which is IEEE 754's \"after rounding\" rule (clause 7.4). From the rounding table this happens at the thresholds"
msgstr "**上溢**依据舍入后的值判定：若舍入后的结果满足 $\\operatorname{top} > e_{\\max}$，则运算上溢，这就是 IEEE 754 的\"舍入后\"规则（第 7.4 条）。由舍入表可知，这发生在以下阈值处"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:316
msgid "because a value in $(\\Omega, \\Omega + \\frac12\\operatorname{ulp})$ rounds to nearest down to $\\Omega$, while the tie $\\Omega + \\frac12\\operatorname{ulp}$ goes to the even neighbour $2^{e_{\\max}+1}$, which lies outside $F$. An overflowing result is $\\pm\\infty$ for the first two groups and $\\pm\\Omega$ for the third, always with `overflow` and `inexact`. In binary16, $\\Omega = 65504$ and $\\frac12\\operatorname{ulp}(\\Omega) = 16$:"
msgstr "因为 $(\\Omega, \\Omega + \\frac12\\operatorname{ulp})$ 中的值就近舍入时向下舍入到 $\\Omega$，而平局值 $\\Omega + \\frac12\\operatorname{ulp}$ 则舍入到偶数邻值 $2^{e_{\\max}+1}$，它位于 $F$ 之外。上溢结果对前两组为 $\\pm\\infty$，对第三组为 $\\pm\\Omega$，并总是伴随 `overflow` 和 `inexact`。在 binary16 中，$\\Omega = 65504$ 且 $\\frac12\\operatorname{ulp}(\\Omega) = 16$："

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:334
msgid "**Tininess.** A nonzero result is tiny when it lies strictly between $\\pm 2^{e_{\\min}}$. IEEE 754-2019 (clause 7.5) allows two readings, and `TininessDetection` selects one:"
msgstr "**微小性。** 非零结果严格位于 $\\pm 2^{e_{\\min}}$ 之间时称为微小的。IEEE 754-2019（第 7.5 条）允许两种解读，由 `TininessDetection` 选择其一："

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:342
msgid "where $\\circ_{p,\\infty}$ rounds to $p$ bits with an unbounded exponent range. The finalizer computes $\\operatorname{top}(r)$ exactly and, for the after-rounding rule, a second split of the same magnitude at the precision shift alone. The two readings differ only for $r$ just below $2^{e_{\\min}}$ that rounds up to it at $p$ bits: for binary16, $r = 2^{-14} - 2^{-27}$ is tiny before rounding but rounds at 11 bits to $2^{-14}$, which is not tiny."
msgstr "其中 $\\circ_{p,\\infty}$ 在无界指数范围下舍入到 $p$ 位。终结器精确计算 $\\operatorname{top}(r)$，并且对于舍入后规则，再仅按精度移位对同一绝对值做第二次拆分。两种解读仅对略低于 $2^{e_{\\min}}$、且在 $p$ 位下向上舍入到它的 $r$ 有所不同：对于 binary16，$r = 2^{-14} - 2^{-27}$ 在舍入前是微小的，但在 11 位下舍入为 $2^{-14}$，后者并不微小。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:349
msgid "**Underflow flag.** Under default exception handling the underflow flag is raised for a tiny result only when it is also inexact. The finalizer returns no flags at all for an exact result, so an exact subnormal (for example any subnormal difference, as shown above) raises nothing. The `binary16` product $2^{-14} \\times (1 - 2^{-11})$ shows the full rule: the exact value $2^{-14} - 2^{-25}$ is tiny under both readings, lies halfway between two subnormals of spacing $2^{-24}$, rounds to the even neighbour $2^{-14}$, the smallest normal, and raises `underflow` and `inexact`, although the encoded result `0x0400` is normal."
msgstr "**下溢标志。** 在默认异常处理下，仅当微小结果同时不精确时才引发下溢标志。终结器对精确结果完全不返回任何标志，因此精确的次正规数（例如如上所示的任意次正规差）不引发任何标志。`binary16` 乘积 $2^{-14} \\times (1 - 2^{-11})$ 展示了完整规则：精确值 $2^{-14} - 2^{-25}$ 在两种解读下都是微小的，它恰好位于间距为 $2^{-24}$ 的两个次正规数的正中间，舍入到偶数邻值 $2^{-14}$（即最小正规数），并引发 `underflow` 和 `inexact`，尽管编码后的结果 `0x0400` 是正规数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:375
msgid "**Far below the range.** A result certainly smaller than $\\eta/2$ in magnitude (decided from exponent bounds without forming it, for example $2^{-10^9} \\cdot 2^{-10^9}$) rounds to $\\pm 0$ or $\\pm\\eta$ according to the direction, with `underflow` and `inexact`. A result certainly above the range goes to the overflow result."
msgstr "**远低于范围。** 绝对值必然小于 $\\eta/2$ 的结果（由指数界判定，无需构造它，例如 $2^{-10^9} \\cdot 2^{-10^9}$）根据舍入方向舍入为 $\\pm 0$ 或 $\\pm\\eta$，并伴随 `underflow` 和 `inexact`。必然高于范围的结果则取上溢结果。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:381
msgid "Signed zeros and NaNs"
msgstr "带符号零与 NaN"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:383
msgid "An exact zero sum $a + b = 0$ with $a, b$ of opposite sign is $+0$ in every direction except RD, where it is $-0$; $(-0) + (-0) = -0$ (clause 6.3). Products and quotients take the exclusive-or of the signs. A NaN operand yields the first NaN operand, quieted, with its sign and payload (clause 6.2.3 allows any input NaN), and `invalid_operation` is raised exactly when an operand is a signaling NaN or the operation is invalid on its own ($\\infty - \\infty$, $0 \\cdot \\infty$, $0/0$, $\\infty/\\infty$, $\\sqrt{x<0}$, $\\operatorname{remainder}(\\infty, y)$, $\\operatorname{remainder}(x, 0)$). Flags are values: `combine` is the bitwise OR, so the flags of a computation form a commutative idempotent monoid and can be accumulated in any order, which a global sticky register cannot offer to concurrent code."
msgstr "$a, b$ 符号相反时的精确零和 $a + b = 0$ 在除 RD 以外的所有方向下均为 $+0$，在 RD 下为 $-0$；$(-0) + (-0) = -0$（第 6.3 条）。积与商取两符号的异或。NaN 操作数产生第一个 NaN 操作数经静默化后的结果，保留其符号和载荷（第 6.2.3 条允许任一输入 NaN），并且当且仅当某个操作数是信号 NaN 或该运算本身无效（$\\infty - \\infty$、$0 \\cdot \\infty$、$0/0$、$\\infty/\\infty$、$\\sqrt{x<0}$、$\\operatorname{remainder}(\\infty, y)$、$\\operatorname{remainder}(x, 0)$）时引发 `invalid_operation`。标志是值：`combine` 是按位或，因此一次计算的标志构成一个交换幂等幺半群，可以按任意顺序累积，而全局粘滞寄存器无法为并发代码提供这一点。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:396
msgid "The elementary functions take the signs of their special values from IEEE 754-2019 §9.2.1, which reads the sign of a zero operand: for example $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, -0) = \\pm\\pi$ but $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, +0) = \\pm 0$, $\\operatorname{tanpi}(n)$ has the sign of $\\operatorname{sinpi}(n)/\\operatorname{cospi}(n)$, and $(-0)^y$ and $(-\\infty)^y$ are negative exactly for an odd integral $y$."
msgstr "初等函数的特殊值符号取自 IEEE 754-2019 §9.2.1，该条款会读取零操作数的符号：例如 $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, -0) = \\pm\\pi$，但 $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, +0) = \\pm 0$；$\\operatorname{tanpi}(n)$ 的符号与 $\\operatorname{sinpi}(n)/\\operatorname{cospi}(n)$ 相同；$(-0)^y$ 与 $(-\\infty)^y$ 恰在 $y$ 为奇整数时为负。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:403
msgid "Far-apart operands in addition"
msgstr "加法中相距很远的操作数"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:405
msgid "**Problem.** $2^{10^9} + 2^{-10^9}$ is exact as a dyadic number, but forming it needs a two-billion-bit coefficient."
msgstr "**问题。** $2^{10^9} + 2^{-10^9}$ 作为二进有理数是精确的，但构造它需要一个二十亿位的系数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:408
msgid "**Choice.** When the leading exponents differ by more than $p + 3$, the sum is formed on the grid with unit $\\upsilon = 2^{e(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$, where $e(\\text{high})$ is the exponent of the last bit of the larger operand, so $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$. The larger operand $H\\upsilon$ is exact on that grid; of the smaller operand only the integer part $L$ of its value in units $\\upsilon$ enters, and if anything below $\\upsilon$ was discarded the magnitude becomes $2(H \\pm L) + 1$ (for subtraction $2(H - L - 1) + 1$) in units of $\\upsilon/2$, that is, one sticky bit at the half unit."
msgstr "**选择。** 当两个操作数的首位指数相差超过 $p + 3$ 时，和在单位为 $\\upsilon = 2^{e(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$ 的网格上构成，其中 $e(\\text{high})$ 是较大操作数最低位的指数，因此 $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$。较大操作数 $H\\upsilon$ 在该网格上是精确的；较小操作数只有其值以 $\\upsilon$ 为单位的整数部分 $L$ 参与运算，若有任何低于 $\\upsilon$ 的部分被丢弃，则以 $\\upsilon/2$ 为单位，幅值变为 $2(H \\pm L) + 1$（减法时为 $2(H - L - 1) + 1$），即在半个单位处放置一个粘滞位。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:418
msgid "**Why it is exact for rounding.** The result has $\\operatorname{top} \\ge \\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - 1$, because the smaller operand is below $2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 2}$. The last retained bit of the rounded result therefore has position at least $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p$ (more on the subnormal grid), and its round bit at least $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 1$. The true sum and the substitute both lie strictly inside the same open interval $\\bigl((H \\pm L)\\upsilon, (H \\pm L + 1)\\upsilon\\bigr)$ (or are equal when nothing was discarded), and that interval lies between two consecutive multiples of $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$, at least two bit positions below the round bit. So $q$ and $g$ agree, and $t$ is set in both cases exactly when something nonzero was discarded. The argument does not need the larger operand to have at most $p$ bits. For subtraction, $H - (L + \\varepsilon) = (H - L - 1) + (1 - \\varepsilon)$ with $0 < 1 - \\varepsilon < 1$, so the same substitution applies to the borrowed form. The complete argument, including the subnormal shift, is in the attachment below."
msgstr "**为何对舍入而言是精确的。** 结果满足 $\\operatorname{top} \\ge \\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - 1$，因为较小操作数低于 $2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 2}$。因此舍入结果保留的最低位的位置至少为 $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p$（在次正规网格上更高），其舍入位至少为 $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 1$。真实的和与替代值都严格位于同一个开区间 $\\bigl((H \\pm L)\\upsilon, (H \\pm L + 1)\\upsilon\\bigr)$ 之内（若没有丢弃任何内容则二者相等），而该区间位于 $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$ 的两个相邻倍数之间，比舍入位至少低两个位位置。因此 $q$ 和 $g$ 一致，且在两种情况下 $t$ 都恰在丢弃了非零内容时被置位。该论证不要求较大操作数至多有 $p$ 位。对于减法，$H - (L + \\varepsilon) = (H - L - 1) + (1 - \\varepsilon)$ 且 $0 < 1 - \\varepsilon < 1$，因此同样的替换也适用于借位形式。包括次正规移位在内的完整论证见下方附件。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:436
msgid "Fused multiply-add"
msgstr "融合乘加"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:438
msgid "`fma_ctx` forms the product $c_x c_y 2^{e_x + e_y}$ exactly as a value whose precision equals its own bit length, and passes it to the addition finalizer, so $x y + z$ is rounded once (clause 5.4.1). The difference from two roundings is the point of the operation: for $a = \\operatorname{RN}(0.1)$ in binary64, the rounding error $a \\cdot a - \\operatorname{RN}(a \\cdot a)$ is lost by `mul_ctx` followed by `sub_ctx` (the second operation sees two equal numbers) but `fma_ctx(a, a, -RN(a·a))` returns it exactly, $-8.33\\ldots \\cdot 10^{-19}$. That the result is exact is Dekker's theorem: the error of a rounded-to-nearest product is itself in $F$ when no underflow occurs (precisely, when $e_a + e_b \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$ for the exponents of the last bits of $a$ and $b$, so the exact product lies on the grid of $F$).[^dekker] If the product exponent leaves the `Int` range, the product either certainly overflows, or it is so small that it acts as a sticky bit next to a nonzero addend; the code places a single bit $p + 9$ positions below the addend's last bit, which by the far-operand argument above rounds identically. With a zero addend such a product is the tiny result of the underflow rule."
msgstr "`fma_ctx` 将乘积 $c_x c_y 2^{e_x + e_y}$ 精确地构造为一个精度等于其自身位长的值，并将其交给加法终结器，因此 $x y + z$ 只舍入一次（第 5.4.1 条）。与两次舍入的区别正是该运算的意义所在：对于 binary64 中的 $a = \\operatorname{RN}(0.1)$，先 `mul_ctx` 再 `sub_ctx` 会丢失舍入误差 $a \\cdot a - \\operatorname{RN}(a \\cdot a)$（第二次运算看到的是两个相等的数），而 `fma_ctx(a, a, -RN(a·a))` 精确地返回它，$-8.33\\ldots \\cdot 10^{-19}$。结果是精确的，这就是 Dekker 定理：在不发生下溢时（确切地说，当 $a$ 和 $b$ 最低位的指数满足 $e_a + e_b \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$，从而精确乘积位于 $F$ 的网格上时），就近舍入乘积的误差本身属于 $F$。[^dekker] 若乘积指数超出 `Int` 范围，则乘积要么必然上溢，要么小到相对非零加数而言只相当于一个粘滞位；代码在加数最低位以下 $p + 9$ 个位置处放置一个单独的位，根据上文关于远距操作数的论证，其舍入结果相同。当加数为零时，这样的乘积就是下溢规则下的微小结果。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:456
msgid "T. J. Dekker, \"A floating-point technique for extending the available precision\", *Numerische Mathematik* 18, 1971; Muller et al., §4.4."
msgstr "T. J. Dekker，\"A floating-point technique for extending the available precision\"，*Numerische Mathematik* 18，1971；Muller 等，§4.4。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:460
msgid "IEEE remainder is exact"
msgstr "IEEE 余数是精确的"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:462
msgid ""
"**Claim.** If $x, y \\in F$ (same precision $p$, same range) and $y \\n"
"e 0$, then $r = x - n y$ with $n = \\operatorname{RNE}_{\\mathbb{Z}}(x/y)$ lies in $F$."
msgstr ""
"**断言。** 若 $x, y \\in F$（精度 $p$ 相同，范围相同）且 $y \\n"
"e 0$，则满足 $n = \\operatorname{RNE}_{\\mathbb{Z}}(x/y)$ 的 $r = x - n y$ 属于 $F$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:466
msgid "**Proof.** Write $x = M_x 2^{q_x}$, $y = M_y 2^{q_y}$ with $|M_x|, |M_y| < 2^p$ and $q_x, q_y \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$. By the choice of $n$, $|r| \\le |y|/2$. If $n = 0$ then $r = x$. Otherwise $|x/y| \\ge \\frac12$, so $|r| \\le |y|/2 \\le |x|$. Now $r$ is an integer multiple of $2^{\\min(q_x, q_y)}$."
msgstr "**证明。** 记 $x = M_x 2^{q_x}$、$y = M_y 2^{q_y}$，其中 $|M_x|, |M_y| < 2^p$ 且 $q_x, q_y \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$。由 $n$ 的选取，$|r| \\le |y|/2$。若 $n = 0$ 则 $r = x$。否则 $|x/y| \\ge \\frac12$，因此 $|r| \\le |y|/2 \\le |x|$。此时 $r$ 是 $2^{\\min(q_x, q_y)}$ 的整数倍。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:472
msgid "If $q_x \\ge q_y$: $r = k 2^{q_y}$ with $|k| 2^{q_y} \\le |M_y| 2^{q_y}/2$, so $|k| < 2^{p-1}$."
msgstr "若 $q_x \\ge q_y$：$r = k 2^{q_y}$，其中 $|k| 2^{q_y} \\le |M_y| 2^{q_y}/2$，因此 $|k| < 2^{p-1}$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:474
msgid "If $q_x < q_y$: $r = k 2^{q_x}$ with $|k| 2^{q_x} \\le |x| = |M_x| 2^{q_x}$, so $|k| < 2^{p}$."
msgstr "若 $q_x < q_y$：$r = k 2^{q_x}$，其中 $|k| 2^{q_x} \\le |x| = |M_x| 2^{q_x}$，因此 $|k| < 2^{p}$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:477
msgid "In both cases $|k| < 2^p$, the exponent is at least $e_{\\min} - p + 1$, and $|r| \\le \\max(|x|, |y|) \\le \\Omega$, so $r \\in F$. $\\square$"
msgstr "两种情形下均有 $|k| < 2^p$，指数至少为 $e_{\\min} - p + 1$，且 $|r| \\le \\max(|x|, |y|) \\le \\Omega$，因此 $r \\in F$。$\\square$"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:480
msgid "The implementation never forms $n$, which can have $2^{30}$ bits. With $X = |x| 2^{-m}$, $Y = |y| 2^{-m}$, $m = \\min(q_x, q_y)$ (integers), it computes $X \\bmod 2Y$ by modular exponentiation of $2^{q_x - q_y}$ when $q_x > q_y$. Writing $X = Q (2Y) + R$, $0 \\le R < 2Y$, gives $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor = 2Q + [R \\ge Y]$, so $R$ alone yields both $X \\bmod Y$ and the parity of $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor$, which is all the ties-to-even choice of $n$ needs. The exact $r$ then goes through the usual finalizer; by the claim, no rounding happens for operands of the context's format."
msgstr "实现从不构造 $n$，它可能有 $2^{30}$ 位。设 $X = |x| 2^{-m}$、$Y = |y| 2^{-m}$、$m = \\min(q_x, q_y)$（均为整数），当 $q_x > q_y$ 时它通过 $2^{q_x - q_y}$ 的模幂计算 $X \\bmod 2Y$。记 $X = Q (2Y) + R$、$0 \\le R < 2Y$，得到 $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor = 2Q + [R \\ge Y]$，因此仅凭 $R$ 即可同时得到 $X \\bmod Y$ 和 $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor$ 的奇偶性，而这正是 $n$ 的偶数优先选择所需的全部信息。精确的 $r$ 随后经由通常的终结器处理；由上述断言，对上下文格式的操作数不会发生舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:490
msgid "Neighbours, scaling and integral values"
msgstr "邻值、缩放与整数值"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:492
msgid "`next_up_ctx(x)` adds a positive step $2^{\\pi - 2}$ to $x$ and rounds toward $+\\infty$, where $\\pi = \\min(e_{\\min} - p,\\ e(x),\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)$. Every gap between consecutive points of $F$ next to $x$ is at least $2^{\\min(e_{\\min} - p + 1,\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)}$ and $x$ itself is a multiple of $2^{e(x)}$, so $x < x + 2^{\\pi - 2} < x^{+}$ for $x \\in F$, and by the definition of RU the result is the least point of $F$ above $x$. The same argument works for an $x$ with more than $p$ bits, which is why such operands are accepted. The flags of this internal addition are discarded, because `nextUp` is quiet (clause 5.3.1) even when it steps from $\\Omega$ to $+\\infty$."
msgstr "`next_up_ctx(x)` 将正步长 $2^{\\pi - 2}$ 加到 $x$ 上并朝 $+\\infty$ 舍入，其中 $\\pi = \\min(e_{\\min} - p,\\ e(x),\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)$。$x$ 旁 $F$ 中相邻点之间的每个间隙都至少为 $2^{\\min(e_{\\min} - p + 1,\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)}$，且 $x$ 本身是 $2^{e(x)}$ 的倍数，因此对 $x \\in F$ 有 $x < x + 2^{\\pi - 2} < x^{+}$，再由 RU 的定义，结果是 $F$ 中高于 $x$ 的最小点。同样的论证对多于 $p$ 位的 $x$ 也成立，这就是此类操作数被接受的原因。这次内部加法的标志被丢弃，因为 `nextUp` 是静默的（第 5.3.1 条），即使它从 $\\Omega$ 步进到 $+\\infty$ 亦然。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:503
msgid "`scaleb_ctx(x, n)` is the finalizer applied to $(c, e + n)$: exact in the normal range, correctly rounded with underflow and overflow outside it. `logb_ctx` returns $\\operatorname{top}(x)$, which is exact and correct for subnormal $x$ because $\\operatorname{top}$ is computed on the integer coefficient. The integral roundings use the same round and sticky bits with $\\sigma = -e$ (the bits below the binary point); `to_int_ctx` and its siblings round first and then compare the integer with the target range, reporting `invalid_operation` instead of returning an implementation-defined sentinel."
msgstr "`scaleb_ctx(x, n)` 是对 $(c, e + n)$ 应用终结器：在正规范围内精确，在范围之外以下溢和上溢正确舍入。`logb_ctx` 返回 $\\operatorname{top}(x)$，它是精确的，并且对次正规的 $x$ 也正确，因为 $\\operatorname{top}$ 是在整数系数上计算的。取整舍入使用相同的舍入位和粘滞位，取 $\\sigma = -e$（即二进制小数点以下的位）；`to_int_ctx` 及其同类先舍入，再将整数与目标范围比较，报告 `invalid_operation` 而非返回由实现定义的哨兵值。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:513
msgid "Decimal conversion"
msgstr "十进制转换"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:515
msgid ""
"**Parsing.** `from_string_ctx` reads $D \\cdot 10^{k}$ exactly ($D$ an integer without trailing zeros). For $|k|$ up to $\\max\\bigl(400, \\lfloor (3n + p)/2 \\rfloor + 64\\bigr)$ ($n$ the number of digits) it is rounded exactly: $D \\cdot 5^{k} \\cdot 2^{k}$ by the dyadic finalizer for $k \\ge 0$, and $D / 5^{|k|} \\cdot 2^{k}$ by the division finalizer for $k < 0$. Beyond that bound it uses directed enclosures $[\\operatorname{RD}_w(D)\\operatorname{RD}_w(10^k), \\operatorname{RU}_w(D)\\operatorname{RU}_w(10^k)]$ at a working precision $w$, doubled until both ends round to the same value with the same flags. The bound makes the loop terminate. The rounding breakpoints of a direction are the points of $F$ (directed modes) or the midpoints between them (nearest modes); both are dyadic with at most $p + 1$ significant bits. For $k \\ge 0$ the odd part of $D 10^{k}$ is a multiple of $5^{k}$, and $5^{k} > 2^{2.32 k} > 2^{p+2}$ beyond the bound, so the value is no breakpoint: $k > \\lfloor (3n+p)/2 \\rfloor + 64 > (p+2)/2.32$. For $k < 0$, $|k| > 1.5n$ gives $5^{|k|} > 10^{n} > D$, so $5^{|k|} \\n"
"mid D$ and $D/10^{|k|}$ is not even dyadic. The points where a flag changes (the overflow threshold, $2^{e_{\\min}}$ for tininess, the points of $F$ for inexactness) are dyadic with at most $p + 1$ significant bits as well. A value that is none of these has a positive distance to all of them, and the enclosure, whose relative width is $O(2^{-w})$, eventually lies strictly between two of them, so some $w$ certifies it; the loop has no attempt limit. Values whose binary logarithm is certainly beyond the range, estimated with $\\log_2 10$ and a safety margin, overflow or underflow without any arithmetic, so `1e100000000` costs nothing."
msgstr ""
"**解析。** `from_string_ctx` 精确读取 $D \\cdot 10^{k}$（$D$ 为不带末尾零的整数）。对于至多 $\\max\\bigl(400, \\lfloor (3n + p)/2 \\rfloor + 64\\bigr)$ 的 $|k|$（$n$ 为数字位数），它被精确舍入：$k \\ge 0$ 时由二进有理终结器处理 $D \\cdot 5^{k} \\cdot 2^{k}$，$k < 0$ 时由除法终结器处理 $D / 5^{|k|} \\cdot 2^{k}$。超出该界后，它在工作精度 $w$ 下使用定向包络 $[\\operatorname{RD}_w(D)\\operatorname{RD}_w(10^k), \\operatorname{RU}_w(D)\\operatorname{RU}_w(10^k)]$，并将精度加倍，直到两端舍入到相同的值且标志相同。该界保证循环终止。某一方向的舍入断点是 $F$ 中的点（定向模式）或它们之间的中点（就近模式）；二者都是至多有 $p + 1$ 位有效位的二进有理数。对于 $k \\ge 0$，$D 10^{k}$ 的奇数部分是 $5^{k}$ 的倍数，且超出该界后 $5^{k} > 2^{2.32 k} > 2^{p+2}$，因此该值不是断点：$k > \\lfloor (3n+p)/2 \\rfloor + 64 > (p+2)/2.32$。对于 $k < 0$，$|k| > 1.5n$ 给出 $5^{|k|} > 10^{n} > D$，因此 $5^{|k|} \\n"
"mid D$，而 $D/10^{|k|}$ 甚至不是二进有理数。标志发生变化的点（上溢阈值、微小性的 $2^{e_{\\min}}$、不精确性的 $F$ 中的点）同样是至多有 $p + 1$ 位有效位的二进有理数。不属于其中任何一类的值到它们都有正的距离，而相对宽度为 $O(2^{-w})$ 的包络最终会严格落在其中两个点之间，因此某个 $w$ 必能完成认证；该循环没有尝试次数上限。以 $\\log_2 10$ 和安全余量估计、其二进制对数必然超出范围的值，无需任何算术即直接上溢或下溢，因此 `1e100000000` 不产生任何开销。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:541
msgid "**Fixed digits.** `to_decimal_string_ctx(x, d)` needs $\\operatorname{round}(x / 10^{E - d + 1})$ with $E = \\lfloor \\log_{10}|x| \\rfloor$. $E$ starts from $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x) \\log_{10} 2 \\rfloor$, which is within one of the answer, and is corrected by comparing $|x|$ with $10^{E+1}$, first through directed bounds of the power and, when they straddle, exactly. The quotient is formed exactly as an integer division when its operands have at most $2^{20}$ bits, so ties and exact results are recognised; otherwise directed enclosures are widened until both ends round to the same integer, which terminates because such a quotient is neither an integer nor a half-integer. A carry into a new leading digit ($9.99 \\to 10.0$) increments $E$ and repeats."
msgstr "**定点位数。** `to_decimal_string_ctx(x, d)` 需要满足 $E = \\lfloor \\log_{10}|x| \\rfloor$ 的 $\\operatorname{round}(x / 10^{E - d + 1})$。$E$ 从 $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x) \\log_{10} 2 \\rfloor$ 开始，它与答案相差不超过一，再通过比较 $|x|$ 与 $10^{E+1}$ 加以校正，先使用幂的定向界，当它们跨越边界时再精确比较。当操作数至多有 $2^{20}$ 位时，商以整数除法精确构成，因此能识别平局和精确结果；否则就加宽定向包络，直到两端舍入到同一个整数，由于这样的商既不是整数也不是半整数，该过程必然终止。进位产生新的最高位数字（$9.99 \\to 10.0$）时，$E$ 加一并重复。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:553
msgid "**Shortest output.** Let $I(x)$ be the set of reals that round to $x$ under RNE in the context; it is an interval containing $x$. For each digit count $n$, the two $n$-digit decimals next to $x$ (truncated and rounded away from zero) are candidates, and a candidate is accepted when parsing it returns $x$, that is when it lies in $I(x)$. Acceptance is monotone in $n$: if the $n$-digit truncation $d_n$ lies in $I(x)$, the $(n+1)$-digit truncation satisfies $d_n \\le d_{n+1} \\le x$ (in magnitude), so it lies in the interval too, and likewise for the upper neighbour. So the least accepted $n$ is found by bisection on $[1, \\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 2]$, an upper bound at which a candidate is always accepted.[^shortest] If both candidates are accepted, the nearer one is chosen, then the even one, which is the nearest decimal of that length. For binary64 this reproduces the host formatter on every value tested."
msgstr "**最短输出。** 设 $I(x)$ 为在该上下文中以 RNE 舍入到 $x$ 的实数集合；它是一个包含 $x$ 的区间。对每个位数 $n$，$x$ 旁的两个 $n$ 位十进制数（截断的和远离零舍入的）是候选值，若解析某候选值返回 $x$，即它位于 $I(x)$ 中，则接受该候选值。接受性关于 $n$ 是单调的：若 $n$ 位截断 $d_n$ 位于 $I(x)$ 中，则 $(n+1)$ 位截断满足 $d_n \\le d_{n+1} \\le x$（按绝对值），因此它也位于该区间内，上侧邻值同理。所以最小的可接受 $n$ 可以通过在 $[1, \\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 2]$（一个候选值总能被接受的上界）上二分查找得到。[^shortest] 若两个候选值都被接受，则选择较近的那个，再选偶数的那个，这就是该长度下最接近的十进制数。对于 binary64，在所有测试过的值上它都与宿主格式化器的输出一致。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:567
msgid "The digit count $\\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 1$ suffices for round trip (Matula 1968; Goldberg 1991, Theorem 15); the extra digit is a margin for the bisection's upper end."
msgstr "位数 $\\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 1$ 足以保证往返转换（Matula 1968；Goldberg 1991，定理 15）；多出的一位是为二分查找上端留的余量。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:573
msgid "**Problem.** For $f = \\exp, \\ln, \\sin, \\ldots$ the value $f(x)$ is transcendental and must be rounded correctly without knowing it."
msgstr "**问题。** 对于 $f = \\exp, \\ln, \\sin, \\ldots$，值 $f(x)$ 是超越数，必须在不知道其值的情况下正确舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:576
msgid "**Options.** Fixed polynomial approximations with a proven error bound (fast, but tied to one precision); Ziv's strategy of evaluating with an a priori error bound and retrying at a higher precision when the rounding is ambiguous;[^ziv] or interval evaluation."
msgstr "**可选方案。** 具有已证明误差界的固定多项式逼近（速度快，但绑定于单一精度）；Ziv 策略，即以先验误差界求值，在舍入有歧义时以更高精度重试；[^ziv] 或区间求值。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:581
msgid ""
"**Choice.** A Ziv loop whose error bound is not estimated but computed: every elementary function evaluates an enclosure $[L, U] \\n"
"i f(x)$ in which every internal operation is rounded downward for $L$ and upward for $U$ at a working precision $w$. If"
msgstr ""
"**选择。** 采用误差界经计算而非估计的 Ziv 循环：每个初等函数在工作精度 $w$ 下求出一个包络 $[L, U] \\n"
"i f(x)$，其中每个内部运算对 $L$ 向下舍入，对 $U$ 向上舍入。若"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:590
msgid "the common value is returned, otherwise $w$ grows. **The value is sound by (R2):** $L \\le f(x) \\le U$ implies $\\circ(L) \\le \\circ(f(x)) \\le \\circ(U)$, so equal ends force $\\circ(f(x)) = \\circ(L)$."
msgstr "则返回该公共值，否则增大 $w$。**由 (R2) 可知该值是可靠的：** $L \\le f(x) \\le U$ 蕴含 $\\circ(L) \\le \\circ(f(x)) \\le \\circ(U)$，因此两端相等必然得到 $\\circ(f(x)) = \\circ(L)$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:594
msgid "The flags need a separate argument. Overflow and tininess (under either rule) depend only on $|r|$ through a threshold, so on one side of zero they are monotone: if $L$ and $U$ (which have the same sign once they round to the same nonzero value) agree, every $r \\in [L, U]$ agrees with them. Inexactness is not monotone: it is false exactly on $F$. If $L < U$ round to the same value $v$ with `inexact`, then $f(x)$ is inexact *unless* $f(x) = v \\in F$. The loop cannot tell these apart, so the flags are right only if every input whose exact result lies in $F$ is caught before the loop. That is why the exact cases below are filtered, and why an exact case that is missed shows up as a spurious `inexact` (nearest rounding) or as a budget failure (directed rounding, where $L$ and $U$ round to different neighbours of $v$)."
msgstr "标志需要单独论证。上溢和微小性（无论采用哪种规则）只通过某个阈值依赖于 $|r|$，因此在零的同一侧它们是单调的：若 $L$ 和 $U$（一旦舍入到同一个非零值，它们就同号）一致，则每个 $r \\in [L, U]$ 都与它们一致。不精确性不是单调的：它恰在 $F$ 上为假。若 $L < U$ 带 `inexact` 舍入到同一个值 $v$，则 $f(x)$ 是不精确的，*除非* $f(x) = v \\in F$。循环无法区分这两种情况，因此只有当每个精确结果位于 $F$ 中的输入都在循环之前被捕获时，标志才是正确的。这就是下文的精确情形要被过滤的原因，也是漏掉的精确情形会表现为虚假的 `inexact`（就近舍入）或预算失败（定向舍入，此时 $L$ 和 $U$ 舍入到 $v$ 的不同相邻值）的原因。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:607
msgid "The enclosures come from series with rigorous tails and from monotone reductions. For $\\exp$ on $[0, 1/8]$, the terms $t_k = x^k/k!$ satisfy $t_{k+1}/t_k = x/(k+1) \\le 1/8$, so after the last summed term $t_n$"
msgstr "包络来自具有严格尾项界的级数以及单调的约简。对于 $[0, 1/8]$ 上的 $\\exp$，各项 $t_k = x^k/k!$ 满足 $t_{k+1}/t_k = x/(k+1) \\le 1/8$，因此在最后一个求和项 $t_n$ 之后"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:615
msgid "and the code stops once $t_n < 2^{-(w+8)}$ and adds $2 t_n$ (rounded upward) to the upper sum; the lower sum of positive terms is already a lower bound. Larger arguments are halved $r$ times and the result squared $r$ times, which is monotone on positive numbers and therefore keeps the enclosure; $e^{-x} = 1/e^{x}$ handles negative arguments. For $\\ln v$ with $v \\in [1, 2]$ the series is"
msgstr "一旦 $t_n < 2^{-(w+8)}$，代码即停止，并将 $2 t_n$（向上舍入）加到上和中；正项的下和本身已是下界。较大的参数先减半 $r$ 次，结果再平方 $r$ 次，平方在正数上是单调的，因此保持包络；$e^{-x} = 1/e^{x}$ 处理负参数。对于满足 $v \\in [1, 2]$ 的 $\\ln v$，级数为"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:626
msgid "with tail $\\sum_{k \\ge m} z^{2k+1}/(2k+1) \\le \\frac{z^{2m+1}}{2m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - z^2}$, the bound the code adds. The trigonometric functions reduce $x$ by an enclosure of $\\pi/2$ (from $\\pi = 4 \\arctan 1$, itself enclosed by the arctangent series after argument halving) at $w \\ge p + \\max(0, \\operatorname{top}(x) + 1) + 96$ bits, so the quadrant $k = \\operatorname{round}(x / (\\pi/2))$ is the same integer at both ends of the enclosure; otherwise the attempt is repeated at a higher precision. This is the Payne–Hanek idea realised by brute precision instead of a stored table of $2/\\pi$; its cost grows with $\\log_2|x|$, so inputs needing more than $10^6$ bits are refused with `ResourceLimit` rather than run for minutes."
msgstr "其尾项为 $\\sum_{k \\ge m} z^{2k+1}/(2k+1) \\le \\frac{z^{2m+1}}{2m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - z^2}$，即代码所加的界。三角函数在 $w \\ge p + \\max(0, \\operatorname{top}(x) + 1) + 96$ 位下用 $\\pi/2$ 的包络（来自 $\\pi = 4 \\arctan 1$，而它本身由参数减半后的反正切级数包络）约简 $x$，使象限 $k = \\operatorname{round}(x / (\\pi/2))$ 在包络两端是同一个整数；否则以更高精度重试。这是以暴力提高精度而非存储 $2/\\pi$ 表格的方式实现的 Payne–Hanek 思想；其代价随 $\\log_2|x|$ 增长，因此需要超过 $10^6$ 位的输入会以 `ResourceLimit` 被拒绝，而不是运行数分钟。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:637
msgid "**Budget.** The loop starts at $w_0 = p + 64$ (for some functions at the operand precision plus 16 when that is larger) and steps $w_{i+1} = w_i + \\max(32, \\lfloor w_i/2 \\rfloor)$, at most 12 attempts. For binary64 the sequence is $117, 175, 262, \\ldots, 10053$ bits."
msgstr "**预算。** 循环从 $w_0 = p + 64$ 开始（对某些函数，若操作数精度加 16 更大则取后者），按 $w_{i+1} = w_i + \\max(32, \\lfloor w_i/2 \\rfloor)$ 递增，至多尝试 12 次。对于 binary64，该序列为 $117, 175, 262, \\ldots, 10053$ 位。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:642
msgid ""
"**Termination.** Ziv's argument has two parts. First, $f(x)$ must not be a breakpoint of $\\circ$ (a point of $F$, a midpoint, or a flag threshold), all of which are dyadic. For a nonzero dyadic $x$, $e^{x}$, $\\sin x$, $\\cos x$, $\\tan x$, the hyperbolic functions, their inverses and $\\ln x$ ($x \\n"
"e 1$) are transcendental by Lindemann–Weierstrass. For $2^x$, $10^x$, $\\log_2 x$ and $\\log_{10} x$ irrationality is enough and elementary: $2^{a/b}$ with $b \\n"
"mid a$ is irrational, so $2^x$ is dyadic only for integral $x$, and $\\log_2 x = a/b$ forces $x = 2^{a/b}$, a power of two; likewise $10^x$ and $\\log_{10} x$ are dyadic only at integral $x \\ge 0$ and at $x = 10^k$. For the $\\pi$-scaled functions Niven's theorem shows that integral, half-integral and (for `tanpi`) quarter-integral arguments are the only dyadic exceptions.[^niven] For `pow` and `rootn` the exceptions are characterised under *Exact powers and roots* below. The exceptions are filtered before the loop: $e^0 = 1$, $\\ln 1 = 0$, $\\log_2 2^k = k$, $2^n$ for integral $|n| < 2^{31}$, $\\sin(\\pm 0)$, the $\\pi$-scaled cases, $10^n$ for integral $0 \\le n \\le \\max(4096, p)$ (beyond that the odd part $5^n$ has more than $p + 1$ bits, so $10^n$ is not a breakpoint), $\\log_{10} 10^n$ for every $n \\ge 1$, dyadic powers and exact roots, and so on."
msgstr ""
"**终止性。** Ziv 的论证分为两部分。第一，$f(x)$ 不能是 $\\circ$ 的断点（$F$ 中的点、中点或标志阈值），而这些都是二进有理数。对于非零二进有理数 $x$，由 Lindemann–Weierstrass 定理，$e^{x}$、$\\sin x$、$\\cos x$、$\\tan x$、双曲函数、它们的反函数以及 $\\ln x$（$x \\n"
"e 1$）都是超越数。对于 $2^x$、$10^x$、$\\log_2 x$ 和 $\\log_{10} x$，无理性就足够了，而且论证是初等的：当 $b \\n"
"mid a$ 时 $2^{a/b}$ 是无理数，因此 $2^x$ 仅在 $x$ 为整数时是二进有理数，而 $\\log_2 x = a/b$ 迫使 $x = 2^{a/b}$ 为 2 的幂；同理，$10^x$ 和 $\\log_{10} x$ 仅在整数 $x \\ge 0$ 和 $x = 10^k$ 处是二进有理数。对于以 $\\pi$ 缩放的函数，Niven 定理表明整数、半整数以及（对 `tanpi`）四分之一整数参数是仅有的二进有理例外。[^niven] 对于 `pow` 和 `rootn`，例外情形在下文*精确幂与根*中刻画。这些例外在循环之前被过滤：$e^0 = 1$、$\\ln 1 = 0$、$\\log_2 2^k = k$、整数 $|n| < 2^{31}$ 的 $2^n$、$\\sin(\\pm 0)$、以 $\\pi$ 缩放的情形、整数 $0 \\le n \\le \\max(4096, p)$ 时的 $10^n$（超出此范围时奇数部分 $5^n$ 多于 $p + 1$ 位，因此 $10^n$ 不是断点）、每个 $n \\ge 1$ 的 $\\log_{10} 10^n$、二进有理数幂和精确根，等等。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:661
msgid "Second, the enclosure must shrink onto $f(x)$ fast enough. The series stop when the next term is below $2^{-(w+8)}$ or $2^{-(w+12)}$ in *absolute* value, which is fine for arguments of moderate size; the width then is $O(2^{-w})$ relative to $f(x)$, a non-breakpoint has a positive distance to every breakpoint, and some $w$ certifies it. Tiny arguments need the two measures under *Tiny arguments* below. How large $w$ must be is the table maker's dilemma: no useful a priori bound is known for arbitrary $p$, so the budget is a resource limit, not a correctness condition. When it runs out the `try_*` form reports a `CertificationFailure` with the stage, the reason and the last $w$, and the total forms return a quiet NaN with `invalid_operation`; neither returns an uncertified value. The pinned MPFR corpus never exhausts it."
msgstr "第二，包络必须足够快地收缩到 $f(x)$ 上。当下一项的*绝对*值低于 $2^{-(w+8)}$ 或 $2^{-(w+12)}$ 时级数停止，这对中等大小的参数没有问题；此时宽度相对于 $f(x)$ 为 $O(2^{-w})$，非断点到每个断点都有正的距离，因此某个 $w$ 能完成认证。微小参数需要下文*微小参数*中的两项措施。$w$ 必须多大，就是制表者困境：对任意 $p$ 都没有已知有用的先验界，因此预算是资源限制，而不是正确性条件。预算耗尽时，`try_*` 形式报告一个 `CertificationFailure`，包含阶段、原因和最后的 $w$，全函数形式则返回带 `invalid_operation` 的静默 NaN；两者都不会返回未经认证的值。固定的 MPFR 语料从未耗尽预算。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:674
msgid "**Exact powers and roots.** An integral exponent with $|y| < 2^{31}$ goes to `pown`. A larger integral $y$ needs no filter: for $x = c \\cdot 2^e$ with $c > 1$ odd, $c^{|y|}$ has more than $2^{31} > p + 1$ bits, and a power of two $2^{ey}$ lies outside every exponent range, so neither is a breakpoint. Every other exponent is $y = m / 2^k$ with $m$ odd and $k \\ge 1$. If $x^y$ is rational, so is $q = x^{|y|}$, and $x^{|m|} = q^{2^k}$; comparing the exponents of $2$ and of each odd prime gives $q = a \\cdot 2^f$ with $a$ odd, $e|m| = f \\cdot 2^k$ and $c^{|m|} = a^{2^k}$. Since $|m|$ is odd, $2^k \\mid e$ and every prime exponent of $c$ is divisible by $2^k$, so $c = r^{2^k}$ and $q = r^{|m|} \\cdot 2^{e|m|/2^k}$. Conversely these values are exact. So a rational `pow` result exists exactly under these two divisibility conditions; for $m > 0$ it is the dyadic $q$, and for $m < 0$ it is $1/q$, which is dyadic only when $r = 1$. Every other `pow` result is irrational. `binary_pow_exact_dyadic` computes the dyadic results and rounds them once, unless the odd part $r^m$ would need more than $2p + 64$ bits (then it has more than $p + 1$ significant bits and is not a breakpoint). The same argument with $1/|n|$ in place of $|y|$ shows that $\\operatorname{rootn}(x, n)$ is rational exactly when $|n| \\mid e$ and $c = r^{|n|}$; `rootn` returns $\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|}$ rounded once for $n > 0$, and for $n < 0$ the correctly rounded quotient $1 / (\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|})$, which division decides with the right `inexact` flag although it need not be dyadic. The perfect-power test has no size limit. It first takes square roots with remainder for every factor $2$ of the degree, stopping at the first nonzero remainder, and then the floor of the remaining odd root: by bisection while the root has at most 64 bits, otherwise by integer Newton steps $r \\leftarrow \\lfloor ((d-1) r + \\lfloor c / r^{d-1} \\rfloor) / d \\rfloor$ started just above the root, which decrease monotonically to $\\lfloor c^{1/d} \\rfloor$; one power $r^d$ then decides exactness. A coefficient with at most $d$ bits other than $1$ is rejected at once, because $r \\ge 2$ gives $r^d \\ge 2^d$."
msgstr "**精确幂与根。** $|y| < 2^{31}$ 的整数指数交给 `pown` 处理。更大的整数 $y$ 无需过滤：对 $x = c \\cdot 2^e$（$c > 1$ 为奇数），$c^{|y|}$ 多于 $2^{31} > p + 1$ 位，而 2 的幂 $2^{ey}$ 位于任何指数范围之外，因此两者都不是断点。其余每个指数都可写成 $y = m / 2^k$，其中 $m$ 为奇数且 $k \\ge 1$。若 $x^y$ 是有理数，则 $q = x^{|y|}$ 也是，并且 $x^{|m|} = q^{2^k}$；比较 $2$ 及每个奇素数的指数可得 $q = a \\cdot 2^f$，其中 $a$ 为奇数，$e|m| = f \\cdot 2^k$ 且 $c^{|m|} = a^{2^k}$。由于 $|m|$ 是奇数，$2^k \\mid e$，且 $c$ 的每个素数指数都能被 $2^k$ 整除，因此 $c = r^{2^k}$ 且 $q = r^{|m|} \\cdot 2^{e|m|/2^k}$。反之，这些值都是精确的。所以有理的 `pow` 结果恰在这两个整除条件下存在；当 $m > 0$ 时它是二进有理数 $q$，当 $m < 0$ 时它是 $1/q$，后者仅在 $r = 1$ 时是二进有理数。其余每个 `pow` 结果都是无理数。`binary_pow_exact_dyadic` 计算这些二进有理结果并只舍入一次，除非奇数部分 $r^m$ 需要多于 $2p + 64$ 位（此时它有多于 $p + 1$ 个有效位，不是断点）。用 $1/|n|$ 代替 $|y|$ 作同样的论证可知，$\\operatorname{rootn}(x, n)$ 恰在 $|n| \\mid e$ 且 $c = r^{|n|}$ 时是有理数；对 $n > 0$，`rootn` 返回只舍入一次的 $\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|}$，对 $n < 0$ 则返回正确舍入的商 $1 / (\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|})$——该商未必是二进有理数，但除法会以正确的 `inexact` 标志判定它。完全幂检测没有大小限制。它先对次数中的每个因子 $2$ 求带余数的平方根，遇到第一个非零余数即停止，然后求剩余奇数次根的下取整：根至多 64 位时用二分法，否则用从略高于根处开始的整数牛顿迭代 $r \\leftarrow \\lfloor ((d-1) r + \\lfloor c / r^{d-1} \\rfloor) / d \\rfloor$，它单调递减到 $\\lfloor c^{1/d} \\rfloor$；随后由一次幂运算 $r^d$ 判定是否精确。除 $1$ 之外至多 $d$ 位的系数会被立即拒绝，因为 $r \\ge 2$ 给出 $r^d \\ge 2^d$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:704
msgid "A negative base with an integral exponent beyond the `pown` range is evaluated as $\\pm|x|^y$. Negation is an exact symmetry of $\\circ$ that swaps the two directed modes, $\\circ_{\\mathrm{RD}}(-v) = -\\circ_{\\mathrm{RU}}(v)$, so for an odd $y$ the code rounds $|x|^y$ with RD and RU exchanged and negates."
msgstr "底数为负、整数指数超出 `pown` 范围时，按 $\\pm|x|^y$ 求值。取负是 $\\circ$ 的一个精确对称，它交换两种定向模式：$\\circ_{\\mathrm{RD}}(-v) = -\\circ_{\\mathrm{RU}}(v)$，因此对奇数 $y$，代码交换 RD 与 RU 来舍入 $|x|^y$，再取负。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:709
msgid "**Tiny arguments.** For small enough $|x|$ (about $2^{-p/2}$ for the odd functions, $2^{-p}$ for $e^x$) the result lies closer to a representable number $a$ than the target spacing: $a = x$ for the odd functions, $a = 1$ for $e^x$, $\\cos$, $\\cosh$. An enclosure whose series stops after its first term then has $a$ itself as one end ($U = x$ for $\\sin$, $L = 1$ for $e^x$), and that end rounds without `inexact` while the other end rounds with it, so the acceptance test alone would only pass once $w$ separates $f(x)$ from $a$, at $w \\approx \\log_2(1/|x|)$ or more. Two measures remove the dependence on $|x|$."
msgstr "**微小参数。** 对足够小的 $|x|$（奇函数约为 $2^{-p/2}$，$e^x$ 约为 $2^{-p}$），结果到某个可表示数 $a$ 的距离小于目标间距：对奇函数 $a = x$，对 $e^x$、$\\cos$、$\\cosh$ 则 $a = 1$。级数在第一项后即停止的包络于是以 $a$ 本身为一端（对 $\\sin$ 为 $U = x$，对 $e^x$ 为 $L = 1$），该端舍入时不带 `inexact`，而另一端舍入时带有它，因此仅靠接受测试，要等到 $w$ 把 $f(x)$ 与 $a$ 区分开时才能通过，即 $w \\approx \\log_2(1/|x|)$ 或更大。两项措施消除了对 $|x|$ 的依赖。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:718
msgid ""
"*Inner endpoints.* Every result that reaches the loop is known not to be a breakpoint. For every function other than `pow` and `rootn`, `binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` replaces an end $E$ that could be a breakpoint (an odd coefficient of at most $p + 1$ bits) by $E' = E \\pm 2^{e_E - s}$ toward the inside of the enclosure, with $s = \\max(1, p + 3 - \\operatorname{bits}(c_E))$. If the leading bit of $E$ is $2^t$, breakpoints near $E$ are at least $2^{t - p - 1}$ apart and the offset is at most $2^{t - p - 2}$, so no breakpoint lies in $(E, E']$. Since $f(x) \\n"
"e E$, either $f(x)$ lies beyond $E'$ or between $E$ and $E'$, and in the second case it shares the open cell between breakpoints with $E'$ and rounds like it. So $\\circ(E') = \\circ(U')$ with equal flags still forces $\\circ(f(x))$ and its flags, and the test passes as soon as the enclosure is narrower than the spacing, independently of $|x|$. `pow` uses inner endpoints whenever its exactness test (above) has shown that the result is irrational, not dyadic, or wider than $p + 1$ bits, so a tiny exponent with $x^y$ closer to $1$ than the target spacing is certified too ($2^{2^{-16000}}$ in binary128 is $1$ with `inexact`). The test leaves a few cases with a power-of-two base undecided (an exponent of magnitude at least $2^{31}$, or a scale outside the 32-bit range); those keep the plain acceptance test."
msgstr ""
"*内端点。* 每个进入循环的结果都已知不是断点。对除 `pow` 和 `rootn` 之外的每个函数，`binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` 把可能是断点的端点 $E$（至多 $p + 1$ 位的奇数系数）替换为朝包络内侧移动的 $E' = E \\pm 2^{e_E - s}$，其中 $s = \\max(1, p + 3 - \\operatorname{bits}(c_E))$。若 $E$ 的最高位为 $2^t$，则 $E$ 附近的断点间隔至少为 $2^{t - p - 1}$，而偏移至多为 $2^{t - p - 2}$，因此 $(E, E']$ 中没有断点。由于 $f(x) \\n"
"e E$，$f(x)$ 要么位于 $E'$ 之外，要么位于 $E$ 与 $E'$ 之间；在后一种情况下，它与 $E'$ 处于断点之间的同一开单元中，舍入结果与之相同。所以标志相同的 $\\circ(E') = \\circ(U')$ 仍然确定 $\\circ(f(x))$ 及其标志，并且只要包络窄于间距测试就会通过，与 $|x|$ 无关。只要 `pow` 的精确性检测（见上文）已表明结果是无理数、不是二进有理数或宽于 $p + 1$ 位，`pow` 就使用内端点，因此 $x^y$ 距 $1$ 比目标间距还近的极小指数也能得到认证（binary128 中的 $2^{2^{-16000}}$ 为 $1$ 并触发 `inexact`）。该检测会留下少数底数为 2 的幂的情形无法判定（指数的绝对值至少为 $2^{31}$，或缩放超出 32 位范围）；这些情形保留普通的接受测试。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:739
msgid "*Tiny-argument bounds.* Some enclosures (for $\\sinh$, $\\tanh$ via $e^x - e^{-x}$, and for $\\operatorname{asinh}$, $\\operatorname{atanh}$, $\\operatorname{asin}$, $\\tan$, `expm1`, `log1p`) straddle the neighbour of $a$ until $w \\approx 3\\log_2(1/|x|)$. For $|x| \\le 1/2$ the series give one-sided bounds with a known side: $0 < x - \\sin x$, $0 < \\tan x - x$, $0 < \\operatorname{asin} x - x$, $0 < \\sinh x - x$, $0 < x - \\tanh x$, $0 < x - \\operatorname{asinh} x$, $0 < \\operatorname{atanh} x - x$, each at most $|x|^3$ (for $x > 0$, mirrored for $x < 0$), and $0 < 1 - \\cos x$, $0 < \\cosh x - 1$, $0 < \\operatorname{expm1}(x) - x$, $0 < x - \\operatorname{log1p}(x)$, each at most $x^2$. With $|x| < 2^T$, `binary_tiny_argument_result` uses the enclosure $[a, a + 2^{\\sigma}]$ or $[a - 2^{\\sigma}, a]$ with $\\sigma = 3T$ (respectively $2T$), raised to at least $t_a - p - 8$, when $\\sigma < t_a - p - 3$ ($2^{t_a}$ the leading bit of $a$), and rounds it with inner endpoints. The condition implies $|x| < 2^{-(p+3)/2} \\le 1/2$, so the bounds apply, and the enclosure is at most a quarter of the breakpoint spacing at $a$ wide. When $a$ is a breakpoint, both ends lie in the cell next to $a$ and the result is decided before the loop; otherwise (an argument wider than $p + 1$ bits) the loop runs as usual. With both measures `sin` and `atan` of $2^{-6000}$ at 53 bits and $e^{2^{-20000}}$ are certified in every rounding mode."
msgstr "*微小参数界。* 某些包络（$\\sinh$、经由 $e^x - e^{-x}$ 的 $\\tanh$，以及 $\\operatorname{asinh}$、$\\operatorname{atanh}$、$\\operatorname{asin}$、$\\tan$、`expm1`、`log1p`）在 $w \\approx 3\\log_2(1/|x|)$ 之前会跨越 $a$ 的相邻值。对 $|x| \\le 1/2$，级数给出方向已知的单侧界：$0 < x - \\sin x$、$0 < \\tan x - x$、$0 < \\operatorname{asin} x - x$、$0 < \\sinh x - x$、$0 < x - \\tanh x$、$0 < x - \\operatorname{asinh} x$、$0 < \\operatorname{atanh} x - x$，各自至多为 $|x|^3$（对 $x > 0$；$x < 0$ 时对称），以及 $0 < 1 - \\cos x$、$0 < \\cosh x - 1$、$0 < \\operatorname{expm1}(x) - x$、$0 < x - \\operatorname{log1p}(x)$，各自至多为 $x^2$。设 $|x| < 2^T$，当 $\\sigma < t_a - p - 3$（$2^{t_a}$ 为 $a$ 的最高位）时，`binary_tiny_argument_result` 使用包络 $[a, a + 2^{\\sigma}]$ 或 $[a - 2^{\\sigma}, a]$，其中 $\\sigma = 3T$（相应地为 $2T$），并提升到至少 $t_a - p - 8$，再用内端点对其舍入。该条件蕴含 $|x| < 2^{-(p+3)/2} \\le 1/2$，因此上述界适用，并且包络宽度至多为 $a$ 处断点间距的四分之一。当 $a$ 是断点时，两端都位于紧邻 $a$ 的单元中，结果在循环之前即已确定；否则（参数宽于 $p + 1$ 位）循环照常运行。借助这两项措施，53 位下 $2^{-6000}$ 的 `sin` 与 `atan` 以及 $e^{2^{-20000}}$ 在每种舍入模式下都能得到认证。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:760
msgid ""
"`rootn` keeps the plain test, and `pow` uses it only for the few results its exactness test cannot classify. For `rootn` it suffices: its enclosure is $e^{\\ln(x)/n}$ at a working precision above the operand precision $q$, and $|\\ln x| / |n| > 2^{-(q + 31)}$ for $x \\n"
"e 1$ and $|n| \\le 10^9$, so an end at $1$ disappears after an attempt or two. `pow` evaluates $e^{y \\ln x}$, where $y$ can be arbitrarily small: an exponent so small that $x^y$ lies closer to $1$ than the target spacing gives an enclosure with $L = 1$ at every affordable $w$. That is why `pow` moves such an end inward once its exactness test has excluded a breakpoint, as described under inner endpoints; for example $2^{2^{-16000}}$ in binary128 is then $1$ with `inexact`."
msgstr ""
"`rootn` 保留普通测试，`pow` 仅对其精确性检测无法分类的少数结果使用普通测试。对 `rootn` 这已足够：其包络是以高于操作数精度 $q$ 的工作精度计算的 $e^{\\ln(x)/n}$，而对 $x \\n"
"e 1$ 和 $|n| \\le 10^9$ 有 $|\\ln x| / |n| > 2^{-(q + 31)}$，因此位于 $1$ 的端点在一两次尝试后就会消失。`pow` 计算 $e^{y \\ln x}$，其中 $y$ 可以任意小：当指数小到使 $x^y$ 到 $1$ 的距离小于目标间距时，在任何可承受的 $w$ 下包络都有 $L = 1$。正因如此，如内端点部分所述，`pow` 在其精确性检测排除断点之后会把这样的端点向内移动；例如 binary128 中的 $2^{2^{-16000}}$ 由此为 $1$ 并触发 `inexact`。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:771
msgid "I. Niven, *Irrational Numbers*, 1956, Corollary 3.12: if $r$ is rational and $\\sin(\\pi r)$ is rational, then $\\sin(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm\\frac12, \\pm 1\\}$; similarly for $\\cos$, and $\\tan(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm 1\\}$. The value $\\pm\\frac12$ needs $r$ with denominator 6 or 3, which is not dyadic."
msgstr "I. Niven，*Irrational Numbers*，1956，推论 3.12：若 $r$ 为有理数且 $\\sin(\\pi r)$ 为有理数，则 $\\sin(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm\\frac12, \\pm 1\\}$；$\\cos$ 同理，以及 $\\tan(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm 1\\}$。值 $\\pm\\frac12$ 需要分母为 6 或 3 的 $r$，而这不是二进有理数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:777
msgid "A. Ziv, \"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\", *ACM TOMS* 17(3), 1991; for interval evaluation see W. Tucker, *Validated Numerics*, Princeton 2011, and F. Johansson, \"Arb: efficient arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius interval arithmetic\", *IEEE Trans. Computers* 66(8), 2017."
msgstr "A. Ziv，\"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\"，*ACM TOMS* 17(3)，1991；区间求值参见 W. Tucker，*Validated Numerics*，Princeton 2011，以及 F. Johansson，\"Arb: efficient arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius interval arithmetic\"，*IEEE Trans. Computers* 66(8)，2017。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:783
msgid "**Integer powers.** `pow_int_ctx` computes $x^n$ by an addition chain at $w = p + \\operatorname{bits}(n) + \\operatorname{bits}(p) + 4$ bits with round-to-nearest. Each chain step $a_k = a_i + a_j$ multiplies two approximations; if $x^{a} \\prod (1 + \\delta)^{E(a)}$ describes the error structure, then $E(a_k) = E(a_i) + E(a_j) + 1$ and $E(1) = 0$, so by induction $E(a) \\le a - 1$. The computed value is therefore $x^n (1 + \\theta)$ with $|\\theta| \\le \\gamma_{n-1} = (n-1)u_w/(1 - (n-1)u_w)$ in Higham's notation, which is below $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n)}$ units in the last place of the $w$-bit result. The code uses the radius $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n) + 2}$ units (one more factor of two for a negative power, whose reciprocal adds $n$ further factors), builds the interval, and accepts when both ends round alike, by the same (R2) argument. When 12 attempts (with $w$ doubled between them) do not certify, the exact power $c^n 2^{ne}$ is formed and rounded, so the result is correctly rounded in every case. A power certainly outside the range is decided first from certified $\\log_2$ bounds; powers of two and powers whose exact value fits in $p$ bits are computed exactly. The Ziv path therefore only sees $c^n$ with $c > 1$ odd and more than $p$ bits, or $1/c^n$, which is not dyadic: neither is in $F$, so the `inexact` it reports is right (the flag argument above). A $c^n$ with exactly $p + 1$ bits is a midpoint; the enclosure then never certifies under nearest rounding and the exact fallback decides it."
msgstr "**整数幂。** `pow_int_ctx` 在 $w = p + \\operatorname{bits}(n) + \\operatorname{bits}(p) + 4$ 位下以就近舍入通过加法链计算 $x^n$。每个链步 $a_k = a_i + a_j$ 将两个近似值相乘；若 $x^{a} \\prod (1 + \\delta)^{E(a)}$ 描述了误差结构，则 $E(a_k) = E(a_i) + E(a_j) + 1$ 且 $E(1) = 0$，由归纳得 $E(a) \\le a - 1$。因此计算值为 $x^n (1 + \\theta)$，用 Higham 的记号即 $|\\theta| \\le \\gamma_{n-1} = (n-1)u_w/(1 - (n-1)u_w)$，它小于 $w$ 位结果的 $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n)}$ 个末位单位。代码使用半径 $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n) + 2}$ 个单位（对负幂再多一个因子 2，其倒数还会再增加 $n$ 个因子），构建区间，并在两端舍入相同时接受，依据同样的 (R2) 论证。若 12 次尝试（每次之间 $w$ 加倍）仍无法认证，则构造精确幂 $c^n 2^{ne}$ 并舍入，因此结果在任何情况下都是正确舍入的。必然超出范围的幂会先依据经认证的 $\\log_2$ 界判定；2 的幂以及精确值能放入 $p$ 位的幂会被精确计算。因此 Ziv 路径只会遇到 $c > 1$ 为奇数且多于 $p$ 位的 $c^n$，或者不是二进有理数的 $1/c^n$：两者都不在 $F$ 中，所以它报告的 `inexact` 是正确的（见上文关于标志的论证）。恰好有 $p + 1$ 位的 $c^n$ 是中点；此时包络在就近舍入下永远无法完成认证，由精确回退来判定。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:805
msgid "**hypot.** `hypot` forms $a^2 + b^2$ exactly from the coefficients and takes one correctly rounded square root, so it needs no loop; the cost is the alignment shift between the two squares. For $|a| \\ge |b| > 0$, $|a| < \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\le |a| + b^2 / (2|a|)$. Write $|a| = c \\cdot 2^e$ with leading bit $2^t$ and $g = 2^{\\min(e,\\, t - p - 1)}$: $|a|$ and every rounding breakpoint near it are multiples of $g$, so when $b^2 < 2|a|g$ no breakpoint lies in $(|a|, |a| + b^2/(2|a|)]$ and every such $b$ gives the same rounded result and flags. $|b| < g/8$ is enough, and `binary_hypot_negligible_operand` then replaces $b$ by $g/8$, which keeps the shift at about twice the operand and target precisions however far apart the exponents are ($\\operatorname{hypot}(1, 2^{-600000}) = 1$ with `inexact`). A shift above $10^6$ bits is still refused as a `certification_failure`; after the replacement it needs a precision near $500\\,000$ bits."
msgstr "**hypot。** `hypot` 由系数精确构成 $a^2 + b^2$，并做一次正确舍入的平方根，因此不需要循环；代价是两个平方之间的对齐移位。对 $|a| \\ge |b| > 0$，有 $|a| < \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\le |a| + b^2 / (2|a|)$。记 $|a| = c \\cdot 2^e$，其最高位为 $2^t$，并令 $g = 2^{\\min(e,\\, t - p - 1)}$：$|a|$ 及其附近的每个舍入断点都是 $g$ 的倍数，因此当 $b^2 < 2|a|g$ 时，$(|a|, |a| + b^2/(2|a|)]$ 中没有断点，每个这样的 $b$ 都给出相同的舍入结果和标志。$|b| < g/8$ 就足够了，此时 `binary_hypot_negligible_operand` 将 $b$ 替换为 $g/8$，这样无论两个指数相距多远，移位都保持在操作数精度与目标精度的约两倍（$\\operatorname{hypot}(1, 2^{-600000}) = 1$，带 `inexact`）。超过 $10^6$ 位的移位仍会作为 `certification_failure` 被拒绝；替换之后，这需要接近 $500\\,000$ 位的精度。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:819
msgid "The coefficient kernel"
msgstr "系数内核"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:821
msgid "**Problem.** Precision costs integer multiplication and division of $p$-bit numbers, and $p$ ranges from 1 to $2^{28}$."
msgstr "**问题。** 精度的代价来自 $p$ 位数的整数乘法和除法，而 $p$ 的范围从 1 到 $2^{28}$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:824
msgid "**Choice.** `BinCoeff` stores up to 128 bits inline and larger values as little-endian 32-bit limbs (a host `bigint` on JavaScript), and dispatches on the shorter operand length $n$ in limbs:"
msgstr "**选择。** `BinCoeff` 将至多 128 位的值内联存储，更大的值存储为小端序的 32 位 limb（在 JavaScript 上为宿主 `bigint`），并按较短操作数的 limb 长度 $n$ 进行分派："

