#~ msgid "Every path returns quotient and remainder satisfying `n = qd + r` and `0 <= r < d`. Square root uses fixed-width kernels through 512 bits and a divide-and-conquer path above that boundary. GCD uses Euclid on small inputs and Lehmer batching once leading-limb quotient prediction can amortize divisions."
